  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.font-stretch</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>text textPath tref tspan</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`font-stretch`** attribute indicates the desired amount of condensing or expansion in the glyphs used to render the text.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute, `font-stretch` can be used as a CSS property. See the {{cssxref("font-stretch", "CSS font-stretch")}} property for more information.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text)
- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
- [tref](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tref)
- [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan)
</Value>
