        <Value>specularConstant</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.baseline-shift</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>textPath tref tspan</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`baseline-shift`** attribute allows repositioning of the dominant-baseline relative to the dominant-baseline of the parent text content element. The shifted object might be a sub- or superscript.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute `baseline-shift` can be used as a CSS property.

&gt; **Note:** This property is going to be deprecated and authors are advised to use [`vertical-align`](/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/vertical-align) instead.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
- [tref](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tref)
- [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>baseline-shift</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.in</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>filter filter feBlend feColorMatrix feComponentTransfer feComposite feConvolveMatrix feDiffuseLighting feDisplacementMap feDropShadow feGaussianBlur feMergeNode feMorphology feOffset feSpecularLighting feTile filter</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`in`** attribute identifies input for the given filter primitive.

The value can be either one of the six keywords defined below, or a string which matches a previous {{SVGAttr("result")}} attribute value within the same [filter](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/filter) element. If no value is provided and this is the first filter primitive, then this filter primitive will use `SourceGraphic` as its input. If no value is provided and this is a subsequent filter primitive, then this filter primitive will use the result from the previous filter primitive as its input.

If the value for {{SVGAttr("result")}} appears multiple times within a given [filter](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/filter) element, then a reference to that result will use the closest preceding filter primitive with the given value for attribute {{SVGAttr("result")}}.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feBlend](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feBlend)
- [feColorMatrix](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feColorMatrix)
- [feComponentTransfer](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feComponentTransfer)
- [feComposite](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feComposite)
- [feConvolveMatrix](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feConvolveMatrix)
- [feDiffuseLighting](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feDiffuseLighting)
- [feDisplacementMap](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feDisplacementMap)
- [feDropShadow](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feDropShadow)
- [feGaussianBlur](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feGaussianBlur)
- [feMergeNode](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feMergeNode)
- [feMorphology](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feMorphology)
- [feOffset](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feOffset)
- [feSpecularLighting](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feSpecularLighting)
- [feTile](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feTile)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>in</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.dur</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>animate animateMotion animateTransform set set</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`dur`** attribute indicates the simple duration of an animation.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [animate](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animate)
- [animateMotion](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateMotion)
- [animateTransform](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateTransform)
- [set](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/set)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 220 150" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;rect x="0" y="0" width="100" height="100"&gt;
    &lt;animate
      attributeType="XML"
      attributeName="y"
      from="0"
      to="50"
      dur="1s"
      repeatCount="indefinite" /&gt;
  &lt;/rect&gt;
  &lt;rect x="120" y="0" width="100" height="100"&gt;
    &lt;animate
      attributeType="XML"
      attributeName="y"
      from="0"
      to="50"
      dur="3s"
      repeatCount="indefinite" /&gt;
  &lt;/rect&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>dur</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.tabindex</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>
        </Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Coreattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`tabindex`** attribute allows you to control whether an element is focusable and to define the relative order of the element for the purposes of sequential focus navigation.

You can use this attribute with any SVG element.
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;?xml version="1.0"?&gt;
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 260 260" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;circle cx="60" cy="60" r="15" tabindex="0" /&gt;
  &lt;circle cx="60" cy="160" r="30" tabindex="0" /&gt;
  &lt;circle cx="160" cy="60" r="30" tabindex="0" /&gt;
  &lt;circle cx="160" cy="160" r="60" tabindex="0" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>tabindex</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.flood-color</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>feFlood feDropShadow</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`flood-color`** attribute indicates what color to use to flood the current filter primitive subregion.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute, `flood-color` can be used as a CSS property.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feFlood](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feFlood)
- [feDropShadow](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feDropShadow)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 420 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;filter id="flood1"&gt;
    &lt;feFlood flood-color="skyblue" x="0" y="0" width="200" height="200" /&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;
  &lt;filter id="flood2"&gt;
    &lt;feFlood flood-color="seagreen" x="0" y="0" width="200" height="200" /&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;

  &lt;rect x="0" y="0" width="200" height="200" style="filter: url(#flood1);" /&gt;
  &lt;rect
    x="0"
    y="0"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    style="filter: url(#flood2); transform: translateX(220px);" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>flood-color</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.marker-end</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>polyline path circle ellipse line path polygon polyline rect marker marker</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`marker-end`** attribute defines the arrowhead or polymarker that will be drawn at the final vertex of the given [shape](/en-US/docs/Web/SVG/Element#shape_elements).

For all shape elements, except [polyline](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polyline) and [path](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/path), the last vertex is the same as the first vertex. In this case, if the value of {{SVGAttr("marker-start")}} and `marker-end` are both not `none`, then two markers will be rendered on that final vertex. For `&lt;path&gt;` elements, for each closed subpath, the last vertex is the same as the first vertex. `marker-end` is only rendered on the final vertex of the [path data](/en-US/docs/Web/SVG/Attribute/d#path_commands).

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute, `marker-end` can be used as a CSS property.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [circle](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/circle)
- [ellipse](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/ellipse)
- [line](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/line)
- [path](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/path)
- [polygon](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polygon)
- [polyline](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polyline)
- [rect](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/rect)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;defs&gt;
    &lt;marker
      id="triangle"
      viewBox="0 0 10 10"
      refX="1"
      refY="5"
      markerUnits="strokeWidth"
      markerWidth="10"
      markerHeight="10"
      orient="auto"&gt;
      &lt;path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill="#f00" /&gt;
    &lt;/marker&gt;
  &lt;/defs&gt;
  &lt;polyline
    fill="none"
    stroke="black"
    points="20,100 40,60 70,80 100,20"
    marker-end="url(#triangle)" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>marker-end</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.fr</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>radialGradient</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`fr`** attribute defines the radius of the focal point for the radial gradient.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [radialGradient](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/radialGradient)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>fr</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.font-size-adjust</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>text textPath tref tspan</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The `font-size-adjust` attribute allows authors to specify an aspect value for an element that will preserve the x-height of the first choice font in a substitute font.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute, `font-size-adjust` can be used as a CSS property. See the {{cssxref("font-size-adjust", "CSS font-size-adjust")}} property for more information.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text)
- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
- [tref](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tref)
- [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg
  width="600"
  height="80"
  viewBox="0 0 500 80"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;text y="20" font-family="Times, serif" font-size="10px"&gt;
    This text uses the Times font (10px), which is hard to read in small sizes.
  &lt;/text&gt;
  &lt;text y="40" font-family="Verdana, sans-serif" font-size="10px"&gt;
    This text uses the Verdana font (10px), which has relatively large lowercase
    letters.
  &lt;/text&gt;
  &lt;text
    y="60"
    font-family="Times, serif"
    font-size="10px"
    font-size-adjust="0.58"&gt;
    This is the 10px Times, but now adjusted to the same aspect ratio as the
    Verdana.
  &lt;/text&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>font-size-adjust</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.y1</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>line linearGradient</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`y1`** attribute is used to specify the first y-coordinate for drawing an SVG element that requires more than one coordinate. Elements that only need one coordinate use the {{SVGAttr("y")}} attribute instead.
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>y1</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.preserveAlpha</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>feConvolveMatrix feConvolveMatrix</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

the `preserveAlpha` attribute indicates how a [feConvolveMatrix](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feConvolveMatrix) element handles alpha transparency.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feConvolveMatrix](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feConvolveMatrix)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 420 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;filter id="convolveMatrix1" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feConvolveMatrix kernelMatrix="1 -1 2 0 0 0 0 0 -2" preserveAlpha="true" /&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;
  &lt;filter id="convolveMatrix2" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feConvolveMatrix
      kernelMatrix="1 -1 2 0 0 0 0 0 -2"
      preserveAlpha="false" /&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;

  &lt;image
    href="mdn_logo_only_color.png"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    style="filter:url(#convolveMatrix1);" /&gt;
  &lt;image
    href="mdn_logo_only_color.png"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    style="filter:url(#convolveMatrix2); transform:translateX(220px);" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>preserveAlpha</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.u1</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>glyph hkern vkern</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`u1`** attribute specifies list of {{Glossary("Unicode")}} characters (refer to the description of the {{SVGAttr("unicode")}} attribute of the [glyph](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/glyph) element for a description of how to express individual Unicode characters) and/or ranges of Unicode characters, which identify a set of possible first {{Glossary("glyph")}} in a kerning pair.

If a given Unicode character within the set has multiple corresponding `&lt;glyph&gt;` elements (i.e., there are multiple `&lt;glyph&gt;` elements with the same `unicode` attribute value but different {{SVGAttr("glyph-name")}} values), then all such glyphs are included in the set. Comma is the separator character; thus, to kern a comma, specify the comma as part of a range of Unicode characters or as a glyph name using the {{SVGAttr("g1")}} attribute. The total set of possible first glyphs in the kerning pair is the union of glyphs specified by the `u1` and `g1` attributes.
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>True</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>u1</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.order</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>feConvolveMatrix feConvolveMatrix</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`order`** attribute indicates the size of the matrix to be used by a [feConvolveMatrix](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feConvolveMatrix) element.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feConvolveMatrix](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feConvolveMatrix)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 420 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;filter id="emboss1" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feTurbulence baseFrequency="0.025" seed="0" /&gt;
    &lt;feConvolveMatrix kernelMatrix="3 0 0 -4" order="2" /&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;
  &lt;filter id="emboss2" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feTurbulence baseFrequency="0.025" seed="0" /&gt;
    &lt;feConvolveMatrix kernelMatrix="3 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 -4" order="3" /&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;

  &lt;rect x="0" y="0" width="200" height="200" style="filter:url(#emboss1);" /&gt;
  &lt;rect
    x="0"
    y="0"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    style="filter:url(#emboss2); transform: translateX(220px);" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>order</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.surfaceScale</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>feDiffuseLighting feSpecularLighting feSpecularLighting feDiffuseLighting</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`surfaceScale`** attribute represents the height of the surface for a light filter primitive.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feDiffuseLighting](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feDiffuseLighting)
- [feSpecularLighting](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feSpecularLighting)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 420 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;filter id="diffuseLighting1" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feDiffuseLighting in="SourceGraphic" surfaceScale="1"&gt;
      &lt;fePointLight x="60" y="60" z="20" /&gt;
    &lt;/feDiffuseLighting&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;
  &lt;filter id="diffuseLighting2" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feDiffuseLighting in="SourceGraphic" surfaceScale="15"&gt;
      &lt;fePointLight x="60" y="60" z="20" /&gt;
    &lt;/feDiffuseLighting&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;

  &lt;rect
    x="0"
    y="0"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    style="filter: url(#diffuseLighting1);" /&gt;
  &lt;rect
    x="0"
    y="0"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    style="filter: url(#diffuseLighting2); transform: translateX(220px);" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>surfaceScale</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.color-interpolation-filters</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>feOffset feImage feTile feFlood feSpotLight feBlend feColorMatrix feComponentTransfer feComposite feConvolveMatrix feDiffuseLighting feDisplacementMap feDropShadow feFlood feGaussianBlur feImage feMerge feMorphology feOffset feSpecularLighting feTile feTurbulence</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`color-interpolation-filters`** attribute specifies the color space for imaging operations performed via filter effects.

&gt; **Note:** This property just has an affect on filter operations. Therefore, it has no effect on filter primitives like [feOffset](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feOffset), [feImage](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feImage), [feTile](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feTile) or [feFlood](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feFlood).
&gt;
&gt; `color-interpolation-filters` has a different initial value than {{SVGAttr("color-interpolation")}}. `color-interpolation-filters` has an initial value of `linearRGB`, whereas `color-interpolation` has an initial value of `sRGB`. Thus, in the default case, filter effects operations occur in the linearRGB color space, whereas all other color interpolations occur by default in the sRGB color space.
&gt;
&gt; It has no affect on filter functions, which operate in the {{Glossary("sRGB")}} color space.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute, `color-interpolation-filters` can be used as a CSS property.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feSpotLight](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feSpotLight)
- [feBlend](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feBlend)
- [feColorMatrix](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feColorMatrix)
- [feComponentTransfer](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feComponentTransfer)
- [feComposite](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feComposite)
- [feConvolveMatrix](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feConvolveMatrix)
- [feDiffuseLighting](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feDiffuseLighting)
- [feDisplacementMap](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feDisplacementMap)
- [feDropShadow](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feDropShadow)
- [feFlood](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feFlood)
- [feGaussianBlur](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feGaussianBlur)
- [feImage](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feImage)
- [feMerge](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feMerge)
- [feMorphology](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feMorphology)
- [feOffset](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feOffset)
- [feSpecularLighting](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feSpecularLighting)
- [feTile](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feTile)
- [feTurbulence](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feTurbulence)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>color-interpolation-filters</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.k1</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>feComposite feComposite</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`k1`** attribute defines one of the values to be used within the `arithmetic` operation of the [feComposite](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feComposite) filter primitive.

The pixel composition is computed using the following formula:

```js
result = k1 * i1 * i2 + k2 * i1 + k3 * i2 + k4;
```

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feComposite](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feComposite)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 420 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;filter id="composite1" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feComposite
      in2="SourceGraphic"
      operator="arithmetic"
      k1="1"
      k2="0"
      k3="0"
      k4="0" /&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;
  &lt;filter id="composite2" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feComposite
      in2="SourceGraphic"
      operator="arithmetic"
      k1="10"
      k2="0"
      k3="0"
      k4="0" /&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;

  &lt;image
    href="mdn.svg"
    x="0"
    y="0"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    style="filter: url(#composite1);" /&gt;
  &lt;image
    href="mdn.svg"
    x="0"
    y="0"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    style="filter: url(#composite2); transform: translateX(220px);" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>k1</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.xChannelSelector</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>feDisplacementMap</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`xChannelSelector`** attribute indicates which color channel from {{SVGAttr("in2")}} to use to displace the pixels in {{SVGAttr("in")}} along the x-axis.
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
