        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>font</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`vert-origin-x`** attribute indicates the x-coordinate in the font coordinate system of the origin of a {{Glossary("glyph")}} to be used when drawing vertically oriented text.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [font](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/font)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
