  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.xlink:type</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>a animate animateMotion animateTransform cursor feImage filter font-face-uri glyphRef image linearGradient mpath pattern radialGradient script set textPath tref use</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>XLinkattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`xlink:type`** attribute identifies the type of {{Glossary("XLink")}} being used. In SVG, only simple links are available.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [a](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/a)
- [animate](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animate)
- [animateMotion](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateMotion)
- [animateTransform](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateTransform)
- [cursor](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/cursor)
- [feImage](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feImage)
- [filter](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/filter)
- [font-face-uri](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/font-face-uri)
- [glyphRef](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/glyphRef)
- [image](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/image)
- [linearGradient](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/linearGradient)
- [mpath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/mpath)
- [pattern](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/pattern)
- [radialGradient](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/radialGradient)
- [script](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/script)
- [set](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/set)
- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
- [tref](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tref)
- [use](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/use)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>True</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>xlink:type</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.visibility</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>a circle ellipse foreignObject image line path polygon polyline rect text textPath tref tspan</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`visibility`** attribute lets you control the visibility of graphical elements. With a value of `hidden` or `collapse` the current graphics element is invisible.

&gt; **Note:** If the `visibility` attribute is set to `hidden` on a text element, then the text is invisible but still takes up space in text layout calculations.

Depending on the value of attribute {{SVGAttr("pointer-events")}}, graphics elements which have their `visibility` attribute set to `hidden` still might receive events.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute, `visibility` can be used as a CSS property. See the {{cssxref("visibility", "CSS visibility")}} property for more information.
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>visibility</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.x2</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>line linearGradient</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`x2`** attribute is used to specify the second x-coordinate for drawing an SVG element that requires more than one coordinate. Elements that only need one coordinate use the {{SVGAttr("x")}} attribute instead.
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>x2</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.type</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>animateTransform feColorMatrix feFuncR feFuncG feFuncB feFuncA feTurbulence style script animateTransform feColorMatrix feFuncA feFuncB feFuncG feFuncR feTurbulence script style animateTransform feColorMatrix feFuncR feFuncG feFuncB feFuncA feTurbulence style script</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Transferfunctionattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The `type` attribute is a generic attribute and it has different meaning based on the context in which it's used.

- For the [animateTransform](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateTransform) element, it defines the type of transformation, whose values change over time.
- For the [feColorMatrix](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feColorMatrix) element, it indicates the type of matrix operation. The keyword `matrix` indicates that a full 5x4 matrix of values will be provided. The other keywords represent convenience shortcuts to allow commonly used color operations to be performed without specifying a complete matrix.
- For the [feFuncR](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feFuncR), [feFuncG](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feFuncG), [feFuncB](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feFuncB), and [feFuncA](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feFuncA) elements, it Indicates the type of component transfer function.
- For the [feTurbulence](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feTurbulence) element, it indicates whether the filter primitive should perform a noise or turbulence function.
- For the [style](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/style) and [script](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/script) elements, it defines the content type of the element.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [animateTransform](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateTransform)
- [feColorMatrix](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feColorMatrix)
- [feFuncA](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feFuncA)
- [feFuncB](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feFuncB)
- [feFuncG](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feFuncG)
- [feFuncR](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feFuncR)
- [feTurbulence](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feTurbulence)
- [script](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/script)
- [style](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/style)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>type</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.stroke-linecap</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>path polyline line text textPath tref tspan</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`stroke-linecap`** attribute is a presentation attribute defining the shape to be used at the end of open subpaths when they are stroked.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute `stroke-linecap` can be used as a CSS property.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [path](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/path)
- [polyline](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polyline)
- [line](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/line)
- [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text)
- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
- [tref](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tref)
- [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 6 6" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;!-- Effect of the (default) "butt" value --&gt;
  &lt;line x1="1" y1="1" x2="5" y2="1" stroke="black" stroke-linecap="butt" /&gt;

  &lt;!-- Effect of the "round" value --&gt;
  &lt;line x1="1" y1="3" x2="5" y2="3" stroke="black" stroke-linecap="round" /&gt;

  &lt;!-- Effect of the "square" value --&gt;
  &lt;line x1="1" y1="5" x2="5" y2="5" stroke="black" stroke-linecap="square" /&gt;

  &lt;!--
  the following pink lines highlight the
  position of the path for each stroke
  --&gt;
  &lt;path d="M1,1 h4 M1,3 h4 M1,5 h4" stroke="pink" stroke-width="0.025" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>stroke-linecap</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.text-rendering</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>text</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`text-rendering`** attribute provides hints to the renderer about what tradeoffs to make when rendering text.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute, `text-rendering` can be used as a CSS property. See the {{cssxref("text-rendering", "CSS text-rendering")}} property for more information.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 140 40" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;text y="15" text-rendering="geometricPrecision"&gt;Geometric precision&lt;/text&gt;
  &lt;text y="35" text-rendering="optimizeLegibility"&gt;Optimized legibility&lt;/text&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>text-rendering</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.descent</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>font-face</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`descent`** attribute defines the maximum unaccented depth of the font.

&gt; **Note:** It was specified to share the syntax and semantics of the obsolete `descent` descriptor of the {{cssxref("@font-face")}} at-rule defined in an early version of CSS 2.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [font-face](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/font-face)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>True</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>descent</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.pointsAtY</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>filter feSpotLight</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`pointsAtY`** attribute represents the y location in the coordinate system established by attribute {{SVGAttr("primitiveUnits")}} on the [filter](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/filter) element of the point at which the light source is pointing.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feSpotLight](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feSpotLight)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 420 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;filter id="lighting1" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feDiffuseLighting in="SourceGraphic"&gt;
      &lt;feSpotLight x="60" y="60" z="50" pointsAtY="0" /&gt;
    &lt;/feDiffuseLighting&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;
  &lt;filter id="lighting2" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feDiffuseLighting in="SourceGraphic"&gt;
      &lt;feSpotLight x="60" y="60" z="50" pointsAtY="400" /&gt;
    &lt;/feDiffuseLighting&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;

  &lt;rect x="0" y="0" width="200" height="200" style="filter: url(#lighting1);" /&gt;
  &lt;rect
    x="0"
    y="0"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    style="filter: url(#lighting2); transform: translateX(220px);" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>pointsAtY</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.by</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>animate animateMotion animateTransform</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`by`** attribute specifies a relative offset value for an attribute that will be modified during an animation.

The starting value for the attribute is either indicated by specifying it as value for the attribute given in the {{SVGAttr("attributeName")}} or the {{SVGAttr("from")}} attribute.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [animate](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animate)
- [animateMotion](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateMotion)
- [animateTransform](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateTransform)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 200 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;rect x="10" y="10" width="100" height="100"&gt;
    &lt;animate attributeName="width" fill="freeze" by="50" dur="3s" /&gt;
  &lt;/rect&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>by</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.k3</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>feComposite feComposite</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`k3`** attribute defines one of the values to be used within the `arithmetic` operation of the [feComposite](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feComposite) filter primitive.

The pixel composition is computed using the following formula:

```js
result = k1 * i1 * i2 + k2 * i1 + k3 * i2 + k4;
```

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feComposite](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feComposite)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 420 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;filter id="composite1" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feComposite
      in2="SourceGraphic"
      operator="arithmetic"
      k1="1"
      k2="0"
      k3="1"
      k4="0" /&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;
  &lt;filter id="composite2" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feComposite
      in2="SourceGraphic"
      operator="arithmetic"
      k1="1"
      k2="0"
      k3="10"
      k4="0" /&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;

  &lt;image
    href="mdn.svg"
    x="0"
    y="0"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    style="filter: url(#composite1);" /&gt;
  &lt;image
    href="mdn.svg"
    x="0"
    y="0"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    style="filter: url(#composite2); transform: translateX(220px);" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>k3</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.height</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>feBlend feColorMatrix feComponentTransfer feComposite feConvolveMatrix feDiffuseLighting feDisplacementMap feDropShadow feFlood feGaussianBlur feImage feMerge feMorphology feOffset feSpecularLighting feTile feTurbulence filter foreignObject image mask pattern rect svg use feBlend feColorMatrix feComponentTransfer feComposite feConvolveMatrix feDiffuseLighting feDisplacementMap feDropShadow feFlood feGaussianBlur feImage feMerge feMorphology feOffset feSpecularLighting feTile feTurbulence filter foreignObject image mask pattern rect svg use</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Filterprimitiveattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`height`** attribute defines the vertical length of an element in the user coordinate system.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feBlend](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feBlend)
- [feColorMatrix](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feColorMatrix)
- [feComponentTransfer](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feComponentTransfer)
- [feComposite](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feComposite)
- [feConvolveMatrix](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feConvolveMatrix)
- [feDiffuseLighting](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feDiffuseLighting)
- [feDisplacementMap](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feDisplacementMap)
- [feDropShadow](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feDropShadow)
- [feFlood](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feFlood)
- [feGaussianBlur](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feGaussianBlur)
- [feImage](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feImage)
- [feMerge](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feMerge)
- [feMorphology](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feMorphology)
- [feOffset](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feOffset)
- [feSpecularLighting](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feSpecularLighting)
- [feTile](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feTile)
- [feTurbulence](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feTurbulence)
- [filter](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/filter)
- [foreignObject](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/foreignObject)
- [image](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/image)
- [mask](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/mask)
- [pattern](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/pattern)
- [rect](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/rect)
- [svg](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/svg)
- [use](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/use)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 300 100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;!-- With a height of 0 or less, nothing will be rendered --&gt;
  &lt;rect y="0" x="0" width="90" height="0" /&gt;
  &lt;rect y="0" x="100" width="90" height="60" /&gt;
  &lt;rect y="0" x="200" width="90" height="100%" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>height</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.version</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>svg svg</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`version`** attribute is used to indicate what specification a SVG document conforms to. It is only allowed on the root [svg](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/svg) element. It is purely advisory and has no influence on rendering or processing.

While it is specified to accept any number, the only two valid choices are currently `1.0` and `1.1`.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [svg](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/svg)

```html
&lt;svg version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 100 100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;rect x="10" y="10" width="80" height="80" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>True</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>version</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
