  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.fill</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>circle ellipse path polygon polyline rect text textPath tref tspan animate animateMotion animateTransform set animate animateMotion animateTransform circle ellipse path polygon polyline rect set text textPath tref tref tspan</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`fill`** attribute has two different meanings. For shapes and text it's a presentation attribute that defines the color (_or any SVG paint servers like gradients or patterns_) used to paint the element; for animation it defines the final state of the animation.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [circle](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/circle)
- [ellipse](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/ellipse)
- [path](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/path)
- [polygon](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polygon)
- [polyline](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polyline)
- [rect](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/rect)
- [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text)
- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
- [tref](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tref)
- [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan)

For animation, these elements are using this attribute: [animate](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animate), [animateMotion](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateMotion), [animateTransform](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateTransform), and [set](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/set).
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 300 100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;!-- Simple color fill --&gt;
  &lt;circle cx="50" cy="50" r="40" fill="pink" /&gt;

  &lt;!-- Fill circle with a gradient --&gt;
  &lt;defs&gt;
    &lt;radialGradient id="myGradient"&gt;
      &lt;stop offset="0%" stop-color="pink" /&gt;
      &lt;stop offset="100%" stop-color="black" /&gt;
    &lt;/radialGradient&gt;
  &lt;/defs&gt;

  &lt;circle cx="150" cy="50" r="40" fill="url(#myGradient)" /&gt;

  &lt;!--
  Keeping the final state of an animated circle
  which is a circle with a radius of 40.
  --&gt;
  &lt;circle cx="250" cy="50" r="20"&gt;
    &lt;animate
      attributeType="XML"
      attributeName="r"
      from="0"
      to="40"
      dur="5s"
      fill="freeze" /&gt;
  &lt;/circle&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
