      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`requiredFeatures`** attribute takes a list of feature strings, with the individual strings separated by white space. It determines whether or not all of the named features are supported by the browser; if all of them are supported, the attribute evaluates to `true` end the element is rendered; otherwise, the attribute evaluates to `false` and the current element and its children are skipped and thus will not be rendered. This provides a way to design SVG that gracefully falls back when features aren't available.

If the attribute is not present, then its implicit evaluated value is `true`. If a null string or empty string value is given to attribute `requiredFeatures`, the attribute is evaluate to `false`.

`requiredFeatures` is often used in conjunction with the [switch](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/switch) element. If `requiredFeatures` is used in other situations, it represents a simple switch on the given element whether to render the element or not.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [a](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/a)
- [animate](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animate)
- [animateMotion](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateMotion)
- [animateTransform](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateTransform)
- [circle](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/circle)
- [clipPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/clipPath)
- [cursor](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/cursor)
- [defs](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/defs)
- [ellipse](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/ellipse)
- [foreignObject](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/foreignObject)
- [g](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/g)
- [image](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/image)
- [line](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/line)
- [mask](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/mask)
- [path](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/path)
- [pattern](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/pattern)
- [polygon](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polygon)
- [polyline](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polyline)
- [rect](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/rect)
- [set](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/set)
- [svg](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/svg)
- [switch](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/switch)
- [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text)
- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
- [tref](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tref)
- [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan)
- [use](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/use)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}

text {
  fill: white;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 250 45" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;g&gt;
    &lt;rect fill="forestgreen" x="10" y="10" height="25" width="230" /&gt;
    &lt;text x="20" y="27"&gt;requiredFeatures supported&lt;/text&gt;
  &lt;/g&gt;
  &lt;g requiredFeatures=""&gt;
    &lt;rect fill="crimson" x="10" y="10" height="25" width="230" /&gt;
    &lt;text x="20" y="27"&gt;requiredFeatures not supported&lt;/text&gt;
  &lt;/g&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>True</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>requiredFeatures</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.fill-rule</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>path polygon polyline text textPath tref tspan</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`fill-rule`** attribute is a presentation attribute defining the algorithm to use to determine the _inside_ part of a shape.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute, `fill-rule` can be used as a CSS property.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [path](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/path)
- [polygon](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polygon)
- [polyline](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polyline)
- [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text)
- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
- [tref](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tref)
- [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="-10 -10 220 120" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;!-- Default value for fill-rule --&gt;
  &lt;polygon
    fill-rule="nonzero"
    stroke="red"
    points="50,0 21,90 98,35 2,35 79,90" /&gt;

  &lt;!--
  The center of the shape has two
  path segments (shown by the red stroke)
  between it and infinity. It is therefore
  considered outside the shape, and not filled.
  --&gt;
  &lt;polygon
    fill-rule="evenodd"
    stroke="red"
    points="150,0 121,90 198,35 102,35 179,90" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>fill-rule</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.display</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>tspan tref tspan tref path path textPath path mask clipPath</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`display`** attribute lets you control the rendering of graphical or container elements.

A value of `display="none"` indicates that the given element and its children will not be rendered. Any value other than `none` or `inherit` indicates that the given element will be rendered by the browser.

When applied to a container element, setting `display` to `none` causes the container and all of its children to be invisible; thus, it acts on groups of elements as a group. This means that any child of an element with `display="none"` will never be rendered even if the child has a value for `display` other than `none`.

When the `display` attribute is set to `none`, then the given element does not become part of the rendering tree. It has implications for the [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan) and [tref](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tref) elements, event processing, for bounding box calculations and for calculation of clipping paths:

- If `display` is set to `none` on a [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan) or [tref](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tref) element, then the text string is ignored for the purposes of text layout.
- Regarding events, if `display` is set to `none`, the element receives no events.
- The geometry of a [graphics element](/en-US/docs/Web/SVG/Element#graphics_elements) with `display` set to `none` is not included in bounding box and clipping paths calculations.

The `display` attribute only affects the direct rendering of a given element, whereas it does not prevent elements from being referenced by other elements. For example, setting it to `none` on a [path](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/path) element will prevent that element from getting rendered directly onto the canvas, but the [path](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/path) element can still be referenced by a [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath) element; furthermore, its geometry will be used in text-on-a-path processing even if the [path](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/path) has a `display` value of `none`.

This attribute also affects direct rendering into offscreen canvases, such as occurs with masks or clip paths. Thus, setting `display="none"` on a child of a [mask](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/mask) will prevent the given child element from being rendered as part of the mask. Similarly, setting `display="none"` on a child of a [clipPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/clipPath) element will prevent the given child element from contributing to the clipping path.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute, `display` can be used as a CSS property. See {{cssxref("display", "CSS display")}} for further information.

You can use this attribute with any SVG element.
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 220 100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;!-- Here the yellow rectangle is displayed --&gt;
  &lt;rect x="0" y="0" width="100" height="100" fill="skyblue"&gt;&lt;/rect&gt;
  &lt;rect x="20" y="20" width="60" height="60" fill="yellow"&gt;&lt;/rect&gt;

  &lt;!-- Here the yellow rectangle is not displayed --&gt;
  &lt;rect x="120" y="0" width="100" height="100" fill="skyblue"&gt;&lt;/rect&gt;
  &lt;rect
    x="140"
    y="20"
    width="60"
    height="60"
    fill="yellow"
    display="none"&gt;&lt;/rect&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>display</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.stroke</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>circle ellipse line path polygon polyline rect text textPath tref tspan</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`stroke`** attribute is a presentation attribute defining the color (_or any SVG paint servers like gradients or patterns_) used to paint the outline of the shape;

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute `stroke` can be used as a CSS property.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [circle](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/circle)
- [ellipse](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/ellipse)
- [line](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/line)
- [path](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/path)
- [polygon](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polygon)
- [polyline](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polyline)
- [rect](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/rect)
- [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text)
- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
- [tref](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tref)
- [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 20 10" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;!-- Simple color stroke --&gt;
  &lt;circle cx="5" cy="5" r="4" fill="none" stroke="green" /&gt;

  &lt;!-- Stroke a circle with a gradient --&gt;
  &lt;defs&gt;
    &lt;linearGradient id="myGradient"&gt;
      &lt;stop offset="0%" stop-color="green" /&gt;
      &lt;stop offset="100%" stop-color="white" /&gt;
    &lt;/linearGradient&gt;
  &lt;/defs&gt;

  &lt;circle cx="15" cy="5" r="4" fill="none" stroke="url(#myGradient)" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>stroke</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.repeatDur</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>animate animateMotion animateTransform set</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`repeatDur`** attribute specifies the total duration for repeating an animation.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [animate](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animate)
- [animateMotion](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateMotion)
- [animateTransform](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateTransform)
- [set](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/set)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 220 150" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;rect x="0" y="0" width="100" height="100"&gt;
    &lt;animate
      attributeType="XML"
      attributeName="y"
      from="0"
      to="50"
      dur="1s"
      repeatDur="5s" /&gt;
  &lt;/rect&gt;
  &lt;rect x="120" y="0" width="100" height="100"&gt;
    &lt;animate
      attributeType="XML"
      attributeName="y"
      from="0"
      to="50"
      dur="1s"
      repeatDur="indefinite" /&gt;
  &lt;/rect&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>repeatDur</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.limitingConeAngle</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>feSpotLight</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`limitingConeAngle`** attribute represents the angle in degrees between the spot light axis (i.e. the axis between the light source and the point to which it is pointing at) and the spot light cone. So it defines a limiting cone which restricts the region where the light is projected. No light is projected outside the cone.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feSpotLight](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feSpotLight)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 480 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;filter id="spotLight1" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feDiffuseLighting diffuseConstant="2"&gt;
      &lt;feSpotLight
        x="10"
        y="10"
        z="50"
        pointsAtX="100"
        pointsAtY="100"
        limitingConeAngle="10" /&gt;
    &lt;/feDiffuseLighting&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;
  &lt;filter id="spotLight2" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feDiffuseLighting diffuseConstant="2"&gt;
      &lt;feSpotLight
        x="10"
        y="10"
        z="50"
        pointsAtX="100"
        pointsAtY="100"
        limitingConeAngle="40" /&gt;
    &lt;/feDiffuseLighting&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;

  &lt;rect
    x="0"
    y="0"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    style="filter: url(#spotLight1);" /&gt;
  &lt;rect
    x="0"
    y="0"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    style="filter: url(#spotLight2); transform: translateX(220px);" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>limitingConeAngle</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.pointsAtZ</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>filter feSpotLight</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`pointsAtZ`** attribute represents the y location in the coordinate system established by attribute {{SVGAttr("primitiveUnits")}} on the [filter](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/filter) element of the point at which the light source is pointing, assuming that, in the initial local coordinate system, the positive z-axis comes out towards the person viewing the content and assuming that one unit along the z-axis equals one unit in x and y.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feSpotLight](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feSpotLight)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 420 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;filter id="lighting1" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feDiffuseLighting in="SourceGraphic"&gt;
      &lt;feSpotLight x="100" y="100" z="50" pointsAtZ="0" /&gt;
    &lt;/feDiffuseLighting&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;
  &lt;filter id="lighting2" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feDiffuseLighting in="SourceGraphic"&gt;
      &lt;feSpotLight x="100" y="100" z="50" pointsAtZ="80" /&gt;
    &lt;/feDiffuseLighting&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;

  &lt;rect x="0" y="0" width="200" height="200" style="filter: url(#lighting1);" /&gt;
  &lt;rect
    x="0"
    y="0"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    style="filter: url(#lighting2); transform: translateX(220px);" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>pointsAtZ</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.fx</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>radialGradient</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`fx`** attribute defines the x-axis coordinate of the focal point for a radial gradient.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [radialGradient](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/radialGradient)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 480 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;defs&gt;
    &lt;radialGradient
      id="gradient1"
      cx="0.5"
      cy="0.5"
      r="0.5"
      fx="0.35"
      fy="0.35"
      fr="5%"&gt;
      &lt;stop offset="0%" stop-color="white" /&gt;
      &lt;stop offset="100%" stop-color="darkseagreen" /&gt;
    &lt;/radialGradient&gt;
    &lt;radialGradient
      id="gradient2"
      cx="0.5"
      cy="0.5"
      r="0.5"
      fx="0.75"
      fy="0.35"
      fr="5%"&gt;
      &lt;stop offset="0%" stop-color="white" /&gt;
      &lt;stop offset="100%" stop-color="darkseagreen" /&gt;
    &lt;/radialGradient&gt;
  &lt;/defs&gt;

  &lt;circle cx="100" cy="100" r="100" fill="url(#gradient1)" /&gt;
  &lt;circle
    cx="100"
    cy="100"
    r="100"
    fill="url(#gradient2)"
    style="transform: translateX(240px);" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>fx</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.horiz-adv-x</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>font glyph missing-glyph font glyph missing-glyph font</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`horiz-adv-x`** attribute indicates the horizontal advance after rendering a {{Glossary("glyph")}} in horizontal orientation.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [font](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/font)
- [glyph](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/glyph)
- [missing-glyph](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/missing-glyph)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
