    <Name>SVG.Attribute.cursor</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>
        </Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

[SVG Attribute reference home](/en-US/docs/Web/SVG/Attribute)

The `cursor` attribute specifies the mouse cursor displayed when the mouse pointer is over an element.

This attribute behaves exactly like the {{ cssxref("cursor","CSS cursor") }} property except that if the browser supports the {{ SVGElement("cursor") }} element, you should be able to use it with the [\&lt;funciri&gt;](/en-US/docs/Web/SVG/Content_type#funciri) notation.

As a presentation attribute, it also can be used as a property directly inside a CSS stylesheet, see {{ cssxref("cursor","CSS cursor") }} for further information.
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>cursor</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.k2</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>feComposite feComposite</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`k2`** attribute defines one of the values to be used within the `arithmetic` operation of the [feComposite](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feComposite) filter primitive.

The pixel composition is computed using the following formula:

```js
result = k1 * i1 * i2 + k2 * i1 + k3 * i2 + k4;
```

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feComposite](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feComposite)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 420 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;filter id="composite1" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feComposite
      in2="SourceGraphic"
      operator="arithmetic"
      k1="1"
      k2="1"
      k3="0"
      k4="0" /&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;
  &lt;filter id="composite2" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feComposite
      in2="SourceGraphic"
      operator="arithmetic"
      k1="1"
      k2="10"
      k3="0"
      k4="0" /&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;

  &lt;image
    href="mdn.svg"
    x="0"
    y="0"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    style="filter: url(#composite1);" /&gt;
  &lt;image
    href="mdn.svg"
    x="0"
    y="0"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    style="filter: url(#composite2); transform: translateX(220px);" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>k2</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.hanging</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>font-face</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`hanging`** attribute indicates the alignment coordinate for {{Glossary("glyph", "glyphs")}} to achieve hanging baseline alignment for horizontally oriented glyph layouts. The value is an offset in the font coordinate system.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [font-face](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/font-face)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>True</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>hanging</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.horiz-origin-y</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>font</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`horiz-origin-y`** attribute indicates the y-coordinate in the font coordinate system of the origin of a {{Glossary("glyph")}} to be used when drawing horizontally oriented text.

&gt; **Note:** The origin applies to all glyphs in the font.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [font](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/font)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>True</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>horiz-origin-y</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.patternContentUnits</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>pattern pattern pattern pattern</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`patternContentUnits`** attribute indicates which coordinate system to use for the contents of the {{ SVGElement("pattern") }} element.

&gt; **Note:** That this attribute has no effect if attribute {{ SVGAttr("viewBox") }} is specified on the {{ SVGElement("pattern") }} element.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [pattern](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/pattern)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 200 100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;!--
  A pattern tile that content coordinates and values are
  computed against the current coordinate user space.
  Note that the size of the tile is computed against
  the bounding box of the target element
  --&gt;
  &lt;pattern
    id="p1"
    width="20%"
    height="20%"
    patternContentUnits="userSpaceOnUse"&gt;
    &lt;circle cx="10" cy="10" r="10" /&gt;
  &lt;/pattern&gt;

  &lt;!--
  A pattern tile that content coordinates and values are
  computed against the bounding box of the target element.
  Note that the size of the tile is also computed against
  the bounding box of the target element
  --&gt;
  &lt;pattern
    id="p2"
    width="20%"
    height="20%"
    patternContentUnits="objectBoundingBox"&gt;
    &lt;circle cx=".1" cy=".1" r=".1" /&gt;
  &lt;/pattern&gt;

  &lt;!-- Left square with user space tiles --&gt;
  &lt;rect x="10" y="10" width="80" height="80" fill="url(#p1)" /&gt;

  &lt;!-- Right square with bounding box tiles --&gt;
  &lt;rect x="110" y="10" width="80" height="80" fill="url(#p2)" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>patternContentUnits</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
