        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`cap-height`** attribute defines the height of uppercase glyphs of the font within the font coordinate system.

&gt; **Note:** It was specified to share the syntax and semantics of the obsolete `cap-height` descriptor of the {{cssxref("@font-face")}} at-rule defined in an early version of CSS 2.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [font-face](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/font-face)
</Value>
