  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.dx</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>feDropShadow feOffset glyphRef text tref tspan feDropShadow filter feOffset filter glyphRef glyphRef text tref tref tspan</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`dx`** attribute indicates a shift along the x-axis on the position of an element or its content.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feDropShadow](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feDropShadow)
- [feOffset](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feOffset)
- [glyphRef](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/glyphRef)
- [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text)
- [tref](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tref)
- [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;!-- Lines materialized the position of the glyphs --&gt;
  &lt;line x1="0" x2="100%" y1="50%" y2="50%" /&gt;
  &lt;line x1="10%" x2="10%" y1="0" y2="100%" /&gt;
  &lt;line x1="60%" x2="60%" y1="0" y2="100%" /&gt;

  &lt;!-- Some reference text --&gt;
  &lt;text x="10%" y="50%" fill="grey"&gt;SVG&lt;/text&gt;

  &lt;!-- The same text with a shift along the x-axis --&gt;
  &lt;text dx="50%" x="10%" y="50%"&gt;SVG&lt;/text&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```
```css
line {
  stroke: red;
  stroke-width: 0.5px;
  stroke-dasharray: 3px;
}
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>dx</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.path</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>animateMotion textPath animateMotion path textPath text</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`path`** attribute has two different meanings, either it defines a text path along which the characters of a text are rendered, or a motion path along which a referenced element is animated.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [animateMotion](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateMotion)
- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;path
    id="MyPath"
    fill="none"
    stroke="silver"
    d="M10,90 Q90,90 90,45 Q90,10 50,10 Q10,10 10,40 Q10,70 45,70 Q70,70 75,50" /&gt;

  &lt;text&gt;
    &lt;textPath
      path="M10,90 Q90,90 90,45 Q90,10 50,10 Q10,10 10,40 Q10,70 45,70 Q70,70 75,50"&gt;
      Quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.
    &lt;/textPath&gt;
  &lt;/text&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>path</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.spreadMethod</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>linearGradient radialGradient</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`spreadMethod`** attribute determines how a shape is filled beyond the defined edges of a gradient.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [linearGradient](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/linearGradient)
- [radialGradient](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/radialGradient)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>spreadMethod</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.href</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>a animate animateMotion animateTransform feImage image linearGradient mpath pattern radialGradient script set textPath use a animate animateMotion animateTransform set feImage image linearGradient radialGradient mpath path pattern pattern radialGradient linearGradient script textPath path textPath use</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Animationtargetelementattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`href`** attribute defines a link to a resource as a reference [URL](/en-US/docs/Web/SVG/Content_type#url). The exact meaning of that link depends on the context of each element using it.

&gt; **Note:** Specifications before SVG 2 defined an {{SVGAttr("xlink:href")}} attribute, which is now rendered obsolete by the `href` attribute. If you need to support earlier browser versions, the deprecated `xlink:href` attribute can be used as a fallback in addition to the `href` attribute, e.g. `&lt;use href="some-id" xlink:href="some-id" x="5" y="5" /&gt;`.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [a](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/a)
- [animate](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animate)
- [animateMotion](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateMotion)
- [animateTransform](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateTransform)
- [feImage](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feImage)
- [image](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/image)
- [linearGradient](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/linearGradient)
- [mpath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/mpath)
- [pattern](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/pattern)
- [radialGradient](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/radialGradient)
- [script](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/script)
- [set](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/set)
- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
- [use](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/use)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 160 40" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/"&gt;
    &lt;text x="10" y="25"&gt;MDN Web Docs&lt;/text&gt;
  &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>href</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.attributeType</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>animate animateTransform set</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Animationattributetargetattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`attributeType`** attribute specifies the namespace in which the target attribute and its associated values are defined.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [animate](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animate)
- [animateTransform](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateTransform)
- [set](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/set)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 250 250" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;rect x="50" y="50" width="100" height="100"&gt;
    &lt;animate
      attributeType="XML"
      attributeName="y"
      from="0"
      to="50"
      dur="5s"
      repeatCount="indefinite" /&gt;
  &lt;/rect&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>True</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>attributeType</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
