  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.vector-effect</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>circle ellipse foreignObject image line path polygon polyline rect text textPath tspan use</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`vector-effect`** property specifies the vector effect to use when drawing an object. Vector effects are applied before any of the other compositing operations, i.e. filters, masks and clips.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute, `vector-effect` can be used as a CSS property.
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>vector-effect</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.stroke-linejoin</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>path polygon polyline rect text textPath tref tspan</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`stroke-linejoin`** attribute is a presentation attribute defining the shape to be used at the corners of paths when they are stroked.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute `stroke-linejoin` can be used as a CSS property.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [path](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/path)
- [polygon](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polygon)
- [polyline](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polyline)
- [rect](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/rect)
- [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text)
- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
- [tref](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tref)
- [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 18 12" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;!--
  Upper left path:
  Effect of the "miter" value
  --&gt;
  &lt;path
    d="M1,5 a2,2 0,0,0 2,-3 a3,3 0 0 1 2,3.5"
    stroke="black"
    fill="none"
    stroke-linejoin="miter" /&gt;

  &lt;!--
  Center path:
  Effect of the "round" value
  --&gt;
  &lt;path
    d="M7,5 a2,2 0,0,0 2,-3 a3,3 0 0 1 2,3.5"
    stroke="black"
    fill="none"
    stroke-linejoin="round" /&gt;

  &lt;!--
  Upper right path:
  Effect of the "bevel" value
  --&gt;
  &lt;path
    d="M13,5 a2,2 0,0,0 2,-3 a3,3 0 0 1 2,3.5"
    stroke="black"
    fill="none"
    stroke-linejoin="bevel" /&gt;

  &lt;!--
  Bottom left path:
  Effect of the "miter-clip" value
  with fallback to "miter" if not supported.
  --&gt;
  &lt;path
    d="M3,11 a2,2 0,0,0 2,-3 a3,3 0 0 1 2,3.5"
    stroke="black"
    fill="none"
    stroke-linejoin="miter-clip" /&gt;

  &lt;!--
  Bottom right path:
  Effect of the "arcs" value
  with fallback to "miter" if not supported.
  --&gt;
  &lt;path
    d="M9,11 a2,2 0,0,0 2,-3 a3,3 0 0 1 2,3.5"
    stroke="black"
    fill="none"
    stroke-linejoin="arcs" /&gt;

  &lt;!--
  the following pink lines highlight the
  position of the path for each stroke
  --&gt;
  &lt;g id="highlight"&gt;
    &lt;path
      d="M1,5 a2,2 0,0,0 2,-3 a3,3 0 0 1 2,3.5"
      stroke="pink"
      fill="none"
      stroke-width="0.025" /&gt;
    &lt;circle cx="1" cy="5" r="0.05" fill="pink" /&gt;
    &lt;circle cx="3" cy="2" r="0.05" fill="pink" /&gt;
    &lt;circle cx="5" cy="5.5" r="0.05" fill="pink" /&gt;
  &lt;/g&gt;
  &lt;use href="#highlight" x="6" /&gt;
  &lt;use href="#highlight" x="12" /&gt;
  &lt;use href="#highlight" x="2" y="6" /&gt;
  &lt;use href="#highlight" x="8" y="6" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>stroke-linejoin</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.text-anchor</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>text tspan tref textPath text textPath tref tspan</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`text-anchor`** attribute is used to align (start-, middle- or end-alignment) a string of pre-formatted text or auto-wrapped text where the wrapping area is determined from the {{cssxref("inline-size")}} property relative to a given point.

This attribute is not applicable to other types of auto-wrapped text. For those cases you should use {{cssxref("text-align")}}. For multi-line text, the alignment takes place for each line.

The `text-anchor` attribute is applied to each individual text chunk within a given [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text) element. Each text chunk has an initial current text position, which represents the point in the user coordinate system resulting from (depending on context) application of the {{SVGAttr("x")}} and {{SVGAttr("y")}} attributes on the `&lt;text&gt;` element, any `x` or `y` attribute values on a [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan) or [tref](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tref) element assigned explicitly to the first rendered character in a text chunk, or determination of the initial current text position for a [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath) element.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute, `text-anchor` can be used as a CSS property.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text)
- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
- [tref](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tref)
- [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;!-- Materialization of anchors --&gt;
  &lt;path
    d="M60,15 L60,110 M30,40 L90,40 M30,75 L90,75 M30,110 L90,110"
    stroke="grey" /&gt;

  &lt;!-- Anchors in action --&gt;
  &lt;text text-anchor="start" x="60" y="40"&gt;A&lt;/text&gt;
  &lt;text text-anchor="middle" x="60" y="75"&gt;A&lt;/text&gt;
  &lt;text text-anchor="end" x="60" y="110"&gt;A&lt;/text&gt;

  &lt;!-- Materialization of anchors --&gt;
  &lt;circle cx="60" cy="40" r="3" fill="red" /&gt;
  &lt;circle cx="60" cy="75" r="3" fill="red" /&gt;
  &lt;circle cx="60" cy="110" r="3" fill="red" /&gt;

  &lt;style&gt;
    &lt;![CDATA[
      text {
        font: bold 36px Verdana, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      }
      ]]&gt;
  &lt;/style&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>text-anchor</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.startOffset</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>textPath textPath textPath</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`startOffset`** attribute defines an offset from the start of the path for the initial current text position along the path after converting the path to the [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath) element's coordinate system.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 220 100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;path
    id="path1"
    fill="none"
    stroke="red"
    d="M10,90 Q90,90 90,45 Q90,10 50,10 Q10,10 10,40 Q10,70 45,70 Q70,70 75,50" /&gt;
  &lt;path
    id="path2"
    fill="none"
    stroke="red"
    d="M130,90 Q210,90 210,45 Q210,10 170,10 Q130,10 130,40 Q130,70 165,70 Q190,70 195,50" /&gt;

  &lt;text&gt;
    &lt;textPath href="#path1" startOffset="0"&gt;
      Quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.
    &lt;/textPath&gt;
  &lt;/text&gt;

  &lt;text&gt;
    &lt;textPath href="#path2" startOffset="40"&gt;
      Quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.
    &lt;/textPath&gt;
  &lt;/text&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>startOffset</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.string</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>font-face-uri font-face-format font-face-uri</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`string`** attribute is a hint to the user agent, and specifies a list of formats that the font referenced by the parent [font-face-uri](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/font-face-uri) element supports.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [font-face-format](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/font-face-format)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>True</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>string</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.width</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>feBlend feColorMatrix feComponentTransfer feComposite feConvolveMatrix feDiffuseLighting feDisplacementMap feDropShadow feFlood feGaussianBlur feImage feMerge feMorphology feOffset feSpecularLighting feTile feTurbulence filter foreignObject image mask pattern rect svg use rect</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`width`** attribute defines the horizontal length of an element in the user coordinate system.
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>width</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.attributeName</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>animate animateTransform set</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`attributeName`** attribute indicates the name of the CSS property or attribute of the target element that is going to be changed during an animation.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [animate](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animate)
- [animateTransform](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateTransform)
- [set](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/set)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 250 250" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;rect x="50" y="50" width="100" height="100"&gt;
    &lt;animate
      attributeType="XML"
      attributeName="y"
      from="0"
      to="50"
      dur="5s"
      repeatCount="indefinite" /&gt;
  &lt;/rect&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>attributeName</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.diffuseConstant</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>feDiffuseLighting</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`diffuseConstant`** attribute represents the k&lt;sub&gt;d&lt;/sub&gt; value in the [Phong lighting model](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phong_reflection_model). In SVG, this can be any non-negative number.

It's used to determine the final RGB value of a given pixel. The brighter the lighting-color, the smaller this number should be.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feDiffuseLighting](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feDiffuseLighting)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 420 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;filter id="diffuseLighting1" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feDiffuseLighting in="SourceGraphic" diffuseConstant="1"&gt;
      &lt;fePointLight x="60" y="60" z="20" /&gt;
    &lt;/feDiffuseLighting&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;
  &lt;filter id="diffuseLighting2" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feDiffuseLighting in="SourceGraphic" diffuseConstant="2"&gt;
      &lt;fePointLight x="60" y="60" z="20" /&gt;
    &lt;/feDiffuseLighting&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;

  &lt;rect
    x="0"
    y="0"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    style="filter: url(#diffuseLighting1);" /&gt;
  &lt;rect
    x="0"
    y="0"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    style="filter: url(#diffuseLighting2); transform: translateX(220px);" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>diffuseConstant</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.marker-mid</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>circle ellipse line path polygon polyline rect marker marker</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`marker-mid`** attribute defines the arrowhead or polymarker that will be drawn at all interior vertices of the given [shape](/en-US/docs/Web/SVG/Element#shape_elements).

The marker is rendered on every vertex other than the first and last vertices of the [path data](/en-US/docs/Web/SVG/Attribute/d#path_commands).

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute, `marker-mid` can be used as a CSS property.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [circle](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/circle)
- [ellipse](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/ellipse)
- [line](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/line)
- [path](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/path)
- [polygon](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polygon)
- [polyline](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polyline)
- [rect](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/rect)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;defs&gt;
    &lt;marker id="circle" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="4" refY="4"&gt;
      &lt;circle cx="4" cy="4" r="4" stroke="none" fill="#f00" /&gt;
    &lt;/marker&gt;
  &lt;/defs&gt;
  &lt;polyline
    fill="none"
    stroke="black"
    points="20,100 40,60 70,80 100,20"
    marker-mid="url(#circle)" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>marker-mid</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.color-profile</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>image image</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`color-profile`** attribute is used to define which color profile a raster image included through the [image](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/image) element should use.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute, `color-profile` can be used as a CSS property.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [image](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/image)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>True</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>color-profile</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.v-alphabetic</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>font-face</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`v-alphabetic`** attribute defines indicates the alignment coordinate for {{Glossary("glyphs")}} to achieve alphabetic baseline alignment. The value is an offset in the font coordinate system relative to the glyph-specific {{SVGAttr("vert-origin-x")}} attribute.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [font-face](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/font-face)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>True</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>v-alphabetic</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.stroke-dashoffset</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>circle ellipse path line polygon polyline rect text textPath tref tspan</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`stroke-dashoffset`** attribute is a presentation attribute defining an offset on the rendering of the associated dash array.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute `stroke-dashoffset` can be used as a CSS property.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [circle](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/circle)
- [ellipse](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/ellipse)
- [path](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/path)
- [line](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/line)
- [polygon](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polygon)
- [polyline](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polyline)
- [rect](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/rect)
- [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text)
- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
- [tref](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tref)
- [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="-3 0 33 10" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;!-- No dash array --&gt;
  &lt;line x1="0" y1="1" x2="30" y2="1" stroke="black" /&gt;

  &lt;!-- No dash offset --&gt;
  &lt;line x1="0" y1="3" x2="30" y2="3" stroke="black" stroke-dasharray="3 1" /&gt;

  &lt;!--
  The start of the dash array computation
  is pulled by 3 user units
  --&gt;
  &lt;line
    x1="0"
    y1="5"
    x2="30"
    y2="5"
    stroke="black"
    stroke-dasharray="3 1"
    stroke-dashoffset="3" /&gt;

  &lt;!--
  The start of the dash array computation
  is pushed by 3 user units
  --&gt;
  &lt;line
    x1="0"
    y1="7"
    x2="30"
    y2="7"
    stroke="black"
    stroke-dasharray="3 1"
    stroke-dashoffset="-3" /&gt;

  &lt;!--
  The start of the dash array computation
  is pulled by 1 user units which ends up
  in the same rendering as the previous example
  --&gt;
  &lt;line
    x1="0"
    y1="9"
    x2="30"
    y2="9"
    stroke="black"
    stroke-dasharray="3 1"
    stroke-dashoffset="1" /&gt;

  &lt;!--
  the following red lines highlight the
  offset of the dash array for each line
  --&gt;
  &lt;path d="M0,5 h-3 M0,7 h3 M0,9 h-1" stroke="rgb(255 0 0 / 50%)" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>stroke-dashoffset</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.elevation</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>feDistantLight</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`elevation`** attribute specifies the direction angle for the light source from the XY plane towards the Z-axis, in degrees. Note that the positive Z-axis points towards the viewer of the content.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feDistantLight](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feDistantLight)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 440 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;filter id="distantLight1"&gt;
    &lt;feDiffuseLighting&gt;
      &lt;feDistantLight elevation="0" /&gt;
    &lt;/feDiffuseLighting&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;
  &lt;filter id="distantLight2"&gt;
    &lt;feDiffuseLighting&gt;
      &lt;feDistantLight elevation="45" /&gt;
    &lt;/feDiffuseLighting&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;

  &lt;circle cx="100" cy="100" r="80" style="filter: url(#distantLight1);" /&gt;
  &lt;circle
    cx="100"
    cy="100"
    r="80"
    style="filter: url(#distantLight2); transform: translateX(240px);" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>elevation</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.xlink:show</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>a</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>XLinkattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`xlink:show`** attribute indicates how a linked resource should be opened and is meant for {{Glossary("XLink")}}-aware processors. In case of a conflict, the {{SVGAttr("target")}} attribute has priority, since it can express a wider range of values.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [a](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/a)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>True</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>xlink:show</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.media</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>style</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`media`** attribute specifies a [media query](/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/CSS_media_queries) that must be matched for a style sheet to apply.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [style](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/style)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 240 220" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;style&gt;
    rect {
      fill: black;
    }
  &lt;/style&gt;
  &lt;style media="all and (min-width: 600px)"&gt;
    rect {
      fill: seagreen;
    }
  &lt;/style&gt;

  &lt;text y="15"&gt;Resize the window to see the effect&lt;/text&gt;
  &lt;rect y="20" width="200" height="200" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
