  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.v-mathematical</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>font-face</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`v-mathematical`** attribute indicates the alignment coordinate for {{Glossary("glyph", "glyphs")}} to achieve mathematical baseline alignment for vertically oriented glyph layouts. The value is an offset in the font coordinate system relative to the glyph-specific {{SVGAttr("vert-origin-x")}} attribute.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [font-face](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/font-face)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>True</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>v-mathematical</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.bias</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>feConvolveMatrix feConvolveMatrix</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`bias`** attribute shifts the range of the filter. After applying the {{SVGAttr("kernelMatrix")}} of the [feConvolveMatrix](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feConvolveMatrix) element to the input image to yield a number and applied the {{SVGAttr("divisor")}} attribute, the `bias` attribute is added to each component. This allows representation of values that would otherwise be clamped to 0 or 1.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feConvolveMatrix](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feConvolveMatrix)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>bias</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.pointsAtX</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>filter feSpotLight</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`pointsAtX`** attribute represents the x location in the coordinate system established by attribute {{SVGAttr("primitiveUnits")}} on the [filter](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/filter) element of the point at which the light source is pointing.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feSpotLight](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feSpotLight)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 420 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;filter id="lighting1" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feDiffuseLighting in="SourceGraphic"&gt;
      &lt;feSpotLight x="60" y="60" z="50" pointsAtX="0" /&gt;
    &lt;/feDiffuseLighting&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;
  &lt;filter id="lighting2" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feDiffuseLighting in="SourceGraphic"&gt;
      &lt;feSpotLight x="60" y="60" z="50" pointsAtX="400" /&gt;
    &lt;/feDiffuseLighting&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;

  &lt;rect x="0" y="0" width="200" height="200" style="filter: url(#lighting1);" /&gt;
  &lt;rect
    x="0"
    y="0"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    style="filter: url(#lighting2); transform: translateX(220px);" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>pointsAtX</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.zoomAndPan</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>svg view</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`zoomAndPan`** attribute specifies whether the SVG document can be magnified and panned.

Magnification in this context means the effect of a supplemental scale and translate transformation on the outermost SVG document fragment.

Panning represents a translation (i.e., a shift) transformation on an SVG document fragment in response to a user interface action.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [svg](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/svg)
- [view](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/view)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg
  viewBox="0 0 200 200"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
  zoomAndPan="disable"&gt;
  &lt;filter id="diffuseLighting" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feDiffuseLighting in="SourceGraphic" zoomAndPan="1"&gt;
      &lt;fePointLight x="60" y="60" z="20" /&gt;
    &lt;/feDiffuseLighting&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;

  &lt;rect
    x="0"
    y="0"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    style="filter: url(#diffuseLighting);" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>True</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>zoomAndPan</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.font-weight</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>text textPath tref tspan</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`font-weight`** attribute refers to the boldness or lightness of the glyphs used to render the text, relative to other fonts in the same font family.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute, `font-weight` can be used as a CSS property. See the {{cssxref("font-weight", "CSS font-weight")}} property for more information.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text)
- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
- [tref](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tref)
- [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 200 30" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;text y="20" font-weight="normal"&gt;Normal text&lt;/text&gt;
  &lt;text x="100" y="20" font-weight="bold"&gt;Bold text&lt;/text&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>font-weight</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.transform-origin</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>
        </Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef()}}

The **`transform-origin`** SVG attribute sets the origin for an item's transformations.

You can use this attribute with any SVG element.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute in SVG, `transform-origin` corresponds in syntax and behavior to the `transform-origin` property in CSS, and can be used as CSS property to style SVG. See the [CSS transform-origin](/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/transform-origin) property for more information.
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>transform-origin</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.kernelMatrix</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>feConvolveMatrix feConvolveMatrix</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`kernelMatrix`** attribute defines the list of numbers that make up the kernel matrix for the [feConvolveMatrix](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feConvolveMatrix) element.

Values are separated by space characters and/or a comma. The number of entries in the list must equal to `&lt;orderX&gt;` by `&lt;orderY&gt;` as defined in the {{SVGAttr("order")}} attribute.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feConvolveMatrix](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feConvolveMatrix)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 420 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;filter id="convolveMatrix1" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feConvolveMatrix kernelMatrix="1 1 0 0 0 0 0 0 -1" /&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;
  &lt;filter id="convolveMatrix2" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feConvolveMatrix kernelMatrix="-1 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 1" /&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;

  &lt;image
    href="mdn_logo_only_color.png"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    style="filter:url(#convolveMatrix1);" /&gt;
  &lt;image
    href="mdn_logo_only_color.png"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    style="filter:url(#convolveMatrix2); transform:translateX(220px);" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>kernelMatrix</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.result</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>filter feBlend feColorMatrix feComponentTransfer feComposite feConvolveMatrix feDiffuseLighting feDisplacementMap feDropShadow feFlood feGaussianBlur feImage feMerge feMorphology feOffset feSpecularLighting feTile feTurbulence filter</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`result`** attribute defines the assigned name for this filter primitive. If supplied, then graphics that result from processing this filter primitive can be referenced by an {{SVGAttr("in")}} attribute on a subsequent filter primitive within the same [filter](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/filter) element. If no value is provided, the output will only be available for re-use as the implicit input into the next filter primitive if that filter primitive provides no value for its `in` attribute.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feBlend](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feBlend)
- [feColorMatrix](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feColorMatrix)
- [feComponentTransfer](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feComponentTransfer)
- [feComposite](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feComposite)
- [feConvolveMatrix](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feConvolveMatrix)
- [feDiffuseLighting](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feDiffuseLighting)
- [feDisplacementMap](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feDisplacementMap)
- [feDropShadow](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feDropShadow)
- [feFlood](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feFlood)
- [feGaussianBlur](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feGaussianBlur)
- [feImage](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feImage)
- [feMerge](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feMerge)
- [feMorphology](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feMorphology)
- [feOffset](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feOffset)
- [feSpecularLighting](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feSpecularLighting)
- [feTile](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feTile)
- [feTurbulence](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feTurbulence)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 220 220" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;filter id="displacementFilter"&gt;
    &lt;feTurbulence
      type="turbulence"
      baseFrequency="0.05"
      numOctaves="2"
      result="turbulence" /&gt;
    &lt;feDisplacementMap
      in2="turbulence"
      in="SourceGraphic"
      scale="50"
      xChannelSelector="R"
      yChannelSelector="G" /&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;

  &lt;circle cx="100" cy="100" r="100" style="filter: url(#displacementFilter)" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>result</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.radius</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>feMorphology filter feMorphology</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`radius`** attribute represents the radius (or radii) for the operation on a given [feMorphology](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feMorphology) filter primitive.

If two numbers are provided, the first number represents the x-radius and the second one the y-radius. If one number is provided, then that value is used for both x and y. The values are in the coordinate system established by the {{SVGAttr("primitiveUnits")}} attribute on the [filter](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/filter) element.

A negative or zero value disables the effect of the given filter primitive (i.e., the result is the filter input image).

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feMorphology](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feMorphology)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>radius</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.k</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>hkern vkern</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`k`** attribute specifies the amount for decreasing the spacing between the two glyphs in a kerning pair.

The value is in the font coordinate system. This attribute is required.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [hkern](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/hkern)
- [vkern](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/vkern)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>True</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>k</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.side</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>textPath</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}{{SeeCompatTable}}

The **`side`** attribute determines the side of a path the text is placed on (relative to the path direction).

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}

text {
  font:
    25px Arial,
    Helvetica,
    sans-serif;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 420 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;text&gt;
    &lt;textPath href="#circle1" side="left"&gt;Text left from the path&lt;/textPath&gt;
  &lt;/text&gt;
  &lt;text&gt;
    &lt;textPath href="#circle2" side="right"&gt;Text right from the path&lt;/textPath&gt;
  &lt;/text&gt;

  &lt;circle
    id="circle1"
    cx="100"
    cy="100"
    r="70"
    fill="transparent"
    stroke="silver" /&gt;
  &lt;circle
    id="circle2"
    cx="320"
    cy="100"
    r="70"
    fill="transparent"
    stroke="silver" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>side</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.ideographic</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>font-face</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`ideographic`** attribute indicates the alignment coordinate for {{Glossary("glyphs")}} to achieve ideographic {{Glossary("baseline/typography", "baseline")}} alignment for horizontally oriented glyph layouts. The value is an offset in the font coordinate system.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [font-face](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/font-face)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>True</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>ideographic</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.spacing</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>textPath</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`spacing`** attribute indicates how the user agent should determine the spacing between typographic characters that are to be rendered along a path.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
