  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.operator</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>feComposite feMorphology feComposite feMorphology</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`operator`** attribute has two meanings based on the context it's used in. Either it defines the compositing or morphing operation to be performed.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feComposite](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feComposite)
- [feMorphology](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feMorphology)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
  font:
    20px Arial,
    Helvetica,
    sans-serif;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 120 70" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;filter id="erode"&gt;
    &lt;feMorphology operator="erode" radius="0.4" /&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;
  &lt;filter id="dilate"&gt;
    &lt;feMorphology operator="dilate" radius="0.8" /&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;

  &lt;text x="0" y="15"&gt;Normal text&lt;/text&gt;
  &lt;text x="0" y="40" filter="url(#erode)"&gt;Thin text&lt;/text&gt;
  &lt;text x="0" y="65" filter="url(#dilate)"&gt;Fat text&lt;/text&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>operator</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.stroke-miterlimit</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>path polygon polyline rect text textPath tref tspan</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`stroke-miterlimit`** attribute is a presentation attribute defining a limit on the ratio of the miter length to the {{ SVGAttr("stroke-width") }} used to draw a miter join. When the limit is exceeded, the join is converted from a miter to a bevel.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute `stroke-miterlimit` can be used as a CSS property.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [path](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/path)
- [polygon](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polygon)
- [polyline](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polyline)
- [rect](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/rect)
- [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text)
- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
- [tref](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tref)
- [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 38 30" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;!-- Impact of the default miter limit --&gt;
  &lt;path
    stroke="black"
    fill="none"
    stroke-linejoin="miter"
    id="p1"
    d="M1,9 l7   ,-3 l7   ,3
       m2,0 l3.5 ,-3 l3.5 ,3
       m2,0 l2   ,-3 l2   ,3
       m2,0 l0.75,-3 l0.75,3
       m2,0 l0.5 ,-3 l0.5 ,3" /&gt;

  &lt;!-- Impact of the smallest miter limit (1) --&gt;
  &lt;path
    stroke="black"
    fill="none"
    stroke-linejoin="miter"
    stroke-miterlimit="1"
    id="p2"
    d="M1,19 l7   ,-3 l7   ,3
       m2, 0 l3.5 ,-3 l3.5 ,3
       m2, 0 l2   ,-3 l2   ,3
       m2, 0 l0.75,-3 l0.75,3
       m2, 0 l0.5 ,-3 l0.5 ,3" /&gt;

  &lt;!-- Impact of a large miter limit (8) --&gt;
  &lt;path
    stroke="black"
    fill="none"
    stroke-linejoin="miter"
    stroke-miterlimit="8"
    id="p3"
    d="M1,29 l7   ,-3 l7   ,3
       m2, 0 l3.5 ,-3 l3.5 ,3
       m2, 0 l2   ,-3 l2   ,3
       m2, 0 l0.75,-3 l0.75,3
       m2, 0 l0.5 ,-3 l0.5 ,3" /&gt;

  &lt;!-- the following pink lines highlight the position of the path for each stroke --&gt;
  &lt;path
    stroke="pink"
    fill="none"
    stroke-width="0.05"
    d="M1, 9 l7,-3 l7,3 m2,0 l3.5,-3 l3.5,3 m2,0 l2,-3 l2,3 m2,0 l0.75,-3 l0.75,3 m2,0 l0.5,-3 l0.5,3
      M1,19 l7,-3 l7,3 m2,0 l3.5,-3 l3.5,3 m2,0 l2,-3 l2,3 m2,0 l0.75,-3 l0.75,3 m2,0 l0.5,-3 l0.5,3
      M1,29 l7,-3 l7,3 m2,0 l3.5,-3 l3.5,3 m2,0 l2,-3 l2,3 m2,0 l0.75,-3 l0.75,3 m2,0 l0.5,-3 l0.5,3" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>stroke-miterlimit</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.lighting-color</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>feDiffuseLighting feSpecularLighting</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`lighting-color`** attribute defines the color of the light source for lighting filter primitives.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feDiffuseLighting](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feDiffuseLighting)
- [feSpecularLighting](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feSpecularLighting)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 420 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;filter id="diffuseLighting1" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feDiffuseLighting in="SourceGraphic" lighting-color="white"&gt;
      &lt;fePointLight x="60" y="60" z="20" /&gt;
    &lt;/feDiffuseLighting&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;
  &lt;filter id="diffuseLighting2" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feDiffuseLighting in="SourceGraphic" lighting-color="blue"&gt;
      &lt;fePointLight x="60" y="60" z="20" /&gt;
    &lt;/feDiffuseLighting&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;

  &lt;rect
    x="0"
    y="0"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    style="filter: url(#diffuseLighting1);" /&gt;
  &lt;rect
    x="0"
    y="0"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    style="filter: url(#diffuseLighting2); transform: translateX(220px);" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
