  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.vert-origin-y</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>font</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`vert-origin-y`** attribute indicates the y-coordinate in the font coordinate system of the origin of a {{Glossary("glyph")}} to be used when drawing vertically oriented text.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [font](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/font)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>True</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>vert-origin-y</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
