        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`id`** attribute assigns a unique name to an element.

You can use this attribute with any SVG element.
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```html
&lt;svg
  width="120"
  height="120"
  viewBox="0 0 120 120"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;style&gt;
    &lt;![CDATA[
      #smallRect {
        stroke: #000066;
        fill: #00cc00;
      }
    ]]&gt;
  &lt;/style&gt;

  &lt;rect id="smallRect" x="10" y="10" width="100" height="100" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>id</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.maskUnits</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>mask mask</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`maskUnits`** attribute indicates which coordinate system to use for the geometry properties of the {{ SVGElement("mask") }} element.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [mask](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/mask)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;mask
    id="myMask1"
    maskUnits="userSpaceOnUse"
    x="20%"
    y="20%"
    width="60%"
    height="60%"&gt;
    &lt;rect fill="black" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%" /&gt;
    &lt;circle fill="white" cx="50" cy="50" r="35" /&gt;
  &lt;/mask&gt;

  &lt;mask
    id="myMask2"
    maskUnits="objectBoundingBox"
    x="20%"
    y="20%"
    width="60%"
    height="60%"&gt;
    &lt;rect fill="black" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%" /&gt;
    &lt;circle fill="white" cx="50" cy="50" r="35" /&gt;
  &lt;/mask&gt;

  &lt;!-- Some reference rect to materialized the mask --&gt;
  &lt;rect id="r1" x="0" y="0" width="45" height="45" /&gt;
  &lt;rect id="r2" x="0" y="55" width="45" height="45" /&gt;
  &lt;rect id="r3" x="55" y="55" width="45" height="45" /&gt;
  &lt;rect id="r4" x="55" y="0" width="45" height="45" /&gt;

  &lt;!-- The first 3 rect are masked with useSpaceOnUse units --&gt;
  &lt;use mask="url(#myMask1)" href="#r1" fill="red" /&gt;
  &lt;use mask="url(#myMask1)" href="#r2" fill="red" /&gt;
  &lt;use mask="url(#myMask1)" href="#r3" fill="red" /&gt;

  &lt;!-- The last rect is masked with objectBoundingBox units --&gt;
  &lt;use mask="url(#myMask2)" href="#r4" fill="red" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>maskUnits</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.stroke-dasharray</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>circle ellipse path line polygon polyline rect text textPath tref tspan</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`stroke-dasharray`** attribute is a presentation attribute defining the pattern of dashes and gaps used to paint the outline of the shape;

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute, `stroke-dasharray` can be used as a CSS property.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [circle](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/circle)
- [ellipse](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/ellipse)
- [path](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/path)
- [line](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/line)
- [polygon](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polygon)
- [polyline](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polyline)
- [rect](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/rect)
- [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text)
- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
- [tref](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tref)
- [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 30 12" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;style&gt;
    line {
      stroke: black;
    }
  &lt;/style&gt;
  &lt;!-- No dashes nor gaps --&gt;
  &lt;line x1="0" y1="1" x2="30" y2="1" /&gt;

  &lt;!-- Dashes and gaps of the same size --&gt;
  &lt;line x1="0" y1="3" x2="30" y2="3" stroke-dasharray="4" /&gt;

  &lt;!-- Dashes and gaps of different sizes --&gt;
  &lt;line x1="0" y1="5" x2="30" y2="5" stroke-dasharray="4 1" /&gt;

  &lt;!-- Dashes and gaps of various sizes with an odd number of values --&gt;
  &lt;line x1="0" y1="7" x2="30" y2="7" stroke-dasharray="4 1 2" /&gt;

  &lt;!-- Dashes and gaps of various sizes with an even number of values --&gt;
  &lt;line x1="0" y1="9" x2="30" y2="9" stroke-dasharray="4 1 2 3" /&gt;

  &lt;!-- Dashes starting with a gap --&gt;
  &lt;line x1="0" y1="11" x2="30" y2="11" stroke-dasharray="0 4 0" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>stroke-dasharray</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.data-*</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>
        </Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`data-*`** SVG attributes are called custom data attributes. They let SVG markup and its resulting DOM share information that standard attributes can't, usually for scripting purposes. Their custom data are available via the {{domxref("SVGElement")}} interface of the element the attributes belong to, with the {{domxref("HTMLElement.dataset")}} property.

The `*` can be replaced by any characters allowed in [XML's rules for names](https://www.w3.org/TR/REC-xml/#NT-Name), with the following restrictions:

- Can't start with `xml`.
- No semicolons (`;`, `U+003A`).
- No capital `A` to `Z` letters.

&gt; **Note:** The {{domxref("HTMLElement.dataset")}} property is a {{domxref("DOMStringMap")}} that provides the attribute `data-test-value` via `SVGElement.dataset.testValue`. Hyphen characters (`-`, `U+002D`) are removed and the next letter is capitalized, resulting in the {{Glossary("camel_case", "camel case")}} format.

You can use this attribute with any SVG element.
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>data-*</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.viewBox</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>marker pattern svg symbol view svg rect circle</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`viewBox`** attribute defines the position and dimension, in user space, of an SVG viewport.

The value of the `viewBox` attribute is a list of four numbers separated by whitespace and/or a comma: `min-x`, `min-y`, `width`, and `height`. `min-x` and `min-y` represent the smallest X and Y coordinates that the `viewBox` may have (the origin coordinates of the `viewBox`) and the `width` and `height` specify the `viewBox` size. The resulting `viewBox` is a rectangle in user space mapped to the bounds of the viewport of an SVG element (not the [browser viewport](/en-US/docs/Glossary/Viewport)).
When an SVG contains a `viewBox` attribute (often in combination with a [`preserveAspectRatio`](/en-US/docs/Web/SVG/Attribute/preserveAspectRatio) attribute), a transform stretches or resizes the SVG viewport to fit a particular container element.
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>viewBox</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.alphabetic</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>font-face</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`alphabetic`** attribute defines the lower baseline of a font. It has the same syntax and semantics as the {{cssxref("@font-face/baseline", "baseline")}} descriptor within an {{cssxref("@font-face")}}.

For horizontally oriented glyph layouts, it indicates the alignment coordinate for glyphs to achieve alphabetic baseline alignment. The value is an offset in the font coordinate system.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [font-face](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/font-face)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>True</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>alphabetic</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.enable-background</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>a defs glyph g marker mask missing-glyph pattern svg switch symbol</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`enable-background`** attribute specifies how the accumulation of the background image is managed.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute, `enable-background` can be used as a CSS property.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [a](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/a)
- [defs](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/defs)
- [glyph](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/glyph)
- [g](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/g)
- [marker](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/marker)
- [mask](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/mask)
- [missing-glyph](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/missing-glyph)
- [pattern](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/pattern)
- [svg](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/svg)
- [switch](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/switch)
- [symbol](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/symbol)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>True</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>enable-background</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.direction</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>text tspan svg textPath text tref tspan</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`direction`** attribute specifies the inline-base direction of a [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text) or [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan) element. It defines the start and end points of a line of text as used by the {{SVGAttr("text-anchor")}} and {{SVGAttr("inline-size")}} properties. It also may affect the direction in which characters are positioned if the {{SVGAttr("unicode-bidi")}} property's value is either `embed` or `bidi-override`.

It applies only to glyphs oriented perpendicular to the inline-base direction, which includes the usual case of horizontally-oriented Latin or Arabic text and the case of narrow-cell Latin or Arabic characters rotated 90 degrees clockwise relative to a top-to-bottom inline-base direction.

In many cases, the bidirectional Unicode algorithm produces the desired result automatically, so this attribute doesn't need to be specified in those cases. For other cases, such as when using right-to-left languages, it may be sufficient to add the `direction` attribute to the outermost [svg](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/svg) element, and allow that direction to inherit to all text elements:

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute, `direction` can be used as a CSS property. See {{cssxref("direction", "CSS direction")}} for further information.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
- [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text)
- [tref](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tref)
- [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg
  viewBox="0 0 600 72"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
  direction="rtl"
  lang="fa"&gt;
  &lt;text x="300" y="50" text-anchor="middle" font-size="36"&gt;
    داستان SVG 1.1 SE طولا ني است.
  &lt;/text&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>direction</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.underline-position</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>
        </Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The `underline-position` attribute represents the ideal vertical position of the underline. The underline position is expressed in the font's coordinate system.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- {{ SVGElement("font-face") }}
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>underline-position</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.orient</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>marker</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`orient`** attribute indicates how a marker is rotated when it is placed at its position on the shape.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [marker](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/marker)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;defs&gt;
    &lt;marker
      id="arrow"
      viewBox="0 0 10 10"
      refX="5"
      refY="5"
      markerWidth="6"
      markerHeight="6"
      orient="auto-start-reverse"&gt;
      &lt;path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" /&gt;
    &lt;/marker&gt;

    &lt;marker
      id="dataArrow"
      viewBox="0 0 10 10"
      refX="5"
      refY="5"
      markerWidth="6"
      markerHeight="6"
      orient="-65deg"&gt;
      &lt;path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill="red" /&gt;
    &lt;/marker&gt;
  &lt;/defs&gt;

  &lt;polyline
    points="10,10 10,90 90,90"
    fill="none"
    stroke="black"
    marker-start="url(#arrow)"
    marker-end="url(#arrow)" /&gt;

  &lt;polyline
    points="15,80 29,50 43,60 57,30 71,40 85,15"
    fill="none"
    stroke="grey"
    marker-start="url(#dataArrow)"
    marker-mid="url(#dataArrow)"
    marker-end="url(#dataArrow)" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
