  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.SVG attribute: crossorigin</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>image feImage</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The crossorigin attribute, valid on the [image](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/image) and [feImage](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feImage) elements, provides support for configuration of the Cross-Origin Resource Sharing ([CORS](/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/CORS)) requests for the element's fetched data.

This table shows possible keywords and their meaning:

| Keyword           | Description                                                                                                       |
| ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `anonymous`       | Client CORS requests for this element will have the credentials flag set to 'same-origin'.                        |
| `use-credentials` | Client CORS requests for this element will have the credentials flag set to 'include'.                            |
| `""`              | Setting the attribute name to an empty value, like `crossorigin` or `crossorigin=""`, is the same as `anonymous`. |

It follows the same processing rules as the HTML attribute [`crossorigin`](/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Global_attributes#crossorigin).
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```html
&lt;svg width="200" height="200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;image
    href="https://example.com/mdn_logo_dark.png"
    height="200"
    width="200"
    crossorigin="use-credentials" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>SVG attribute: crossorigin</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.stdDeviation</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>feGaussianBlur</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`stdDeviation`** attribute defines the standard deviation for the blur operation.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feGaussianBlur](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feGaussianBlur)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 480 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;filter id="gaussianBlur1"&gt;
    &lt;feGaussianBlur stdDeviation="1" /&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;
  &lt;filter id="gaussianBlur2"&gt;
    &lt;feGaussianBlur stdDeviation="5" /&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;
  &lt;filter id="gaussianBlur3" x="-30%" y="-30%" width="160%" height="160%"&gt;
    &lt;feGaussianBlur stdDeviation="10" /&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;

  &lt;circle cx="100" cy="100" r="50" style="filter: url(#gaussianBlur1);" /&gt;
  &lt;circle
    cx="100"
    cy="100"
    r="50"
    style="filter: url(#gaussianBlur2); transform: translateX(140px);" /&gt;
  &lt;circle
    cx="100"
    cy="100"
    r="50"
    style="filter: url(#gaussianBlur3); transform: translateX(280px);" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>stdDeviation</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.font-variant</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>text textPath tref tspan</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`font-variant`** attribute indicates whether the text is to be rendered using variations of the font's {{Glossary("glyph", "glyphs")}}.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute, `font-variant` can be used as a CSS property. See the {{cssxref("font-variant", "CSS font-variant")}} property for more information.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text)
- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
- [tref](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tref)
- [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 250 30" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;text y="20" font-variant="normal"&gt;Normal text&lt;/text&gt;
  &lt;text x="100" y="20" font-variant="small-caps"&gt;Small-caps text&lt;/text&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>font-variant</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.numOctaves</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>feTurbulence feTurbulence</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`numOctaves`** attribute defines the number of octaves for the noise function of the [feTurbulence](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feTurbulence) primitive.

An octave is a noise function defined by its frequency and amplitude. A turbulence is built by accumulating several octaves with increasing frequencies and decreasing amplitudes.
The higher the number of octaves, the more natural the noise looks. Though more octaves also require more calculations, resulting in a negative impact on performance.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feTurbulence](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feTurbulence)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 420 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;filter id="noise1" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feTurbulence baseFrequency="0.025" numOctaves="1" /&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;
  &lt;filter id="noise2" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feTurbulence baseFrequency="0.025" numOctaves="3" /&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;

  &lt;rect x="0" y="0" width="200" height="200" style="filter: url(#noise1);" /&gt;
  &lt;rect
    x="0"
    y="0"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    style="filter: url(#noise2); transform: translateX(220px);" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>numOctaves</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.x1</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>line linearGradient</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`x1`** attribute is used to specify the first x-coordinate for drawing an SVG element that requires more than one coordinate. Elements that only need one coordinate use the {{SVGAttr("x")}} attribute instead.
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
