        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.vert-adv-y</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>font glyph missing-glyph font glyph missing-glyph font</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`vert-adv-y`** attribute indicates the vertical advance after rendering a {{Glossary("glyph")}} in vertical orientation.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [font](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/font)
- [glyph](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/glyph)
- [missing-glyph](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/missing-glyph)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>True</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>vert-adv-y</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.keySplines</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>animate animateMotion animateTransform</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`keySplines`** attribute defines a set of [Bézier curve](/en-US/docs/Glossary/Bezier_curve) control points associated with the {{SVGAttr("keyTimes")}} list, defining a cubic Bézier function that controls interval pacing.

This attribute is ignored unless the {{SVGAttr("calcMode")}} attribute is set to `spline`.

If there are any errors in the keySplines specification (bad values, too many or too few values), the animation will not occur.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [animate](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animate)
- [animateMotion](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateMotion)
- [animateTransform](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateTransform)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;circle cx="60" cy="10" r="10"&gt;
    &lt;animate
      attributeName="cx"
      dur="4s"
      calcMode="spline"
      repeatCount="indefinite"
      values="60; 110; 60; 10; 60"
      keyTimes="0; 0.25; 0.5; 0.75; 1"
      keySplines="0.5 0 0.5 1; 0.5 0 0.5 1; 0.5 0 0.5 1; 0.5 0 0.5 1" /&gt;
    &lt;animate
      attributeName="cy"
      dur="4s"
      calcMode="spline"
      repeatCount="indefinite"
      values="10; 60; 110; 60; 10"
      keyTimes="0; 0.25; 0.5; 0.75; 1"
      keySplines="0.5 0 0.5 1; 0.5 0 0.5 1; 0.5 0 0.5 1; 0.5 0 0.5 1" /&gt;
  &lt;/circle&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>keySplines</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.style</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>style</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Coreattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`style`** attribute allows to style an element using {{Glossary("CSS")}} declarations. It functions identically to [the `style` attribute in HTML](/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Global_attributes/style).

You can use this attribute with any SVG element.
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 100 60" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;rect
    width="80"
    height="40"
    x="10"
    y="10"
    style="fill: skyblue; stroke: cadetblue; stroke-width: 2;" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>style</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
