  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.color-interpolation</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>a animate circle clipPath defs ellipse foreignObject g glyph image line linearGradient marker mask missing-glyph path pattern polygon polyline radialGradient rect svg switch symbol text textPath tspan use rect linearGradient radialGradient linearGradient radialGradient</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`color-interpolation`** attribute specifies the color space for gradient interpolations, color animations, and alpha compositing.

&gt; **Note:** For filter effects, the {{SVGAttr("color-interpolation-filters")}} property controls which color space is used.

The color-interpolation property chooses between color operations occurring in the sRGB color space or in a (light energy linear) linearized RGB color space. Having chosen the appropriate color space, component-wise linear interpolation is used.

When a child element is blended into a background, the value of the `color-interpolation` property on the child determines the type of blending, not the value of the `color-interpolation` on the parent. For gradients which make use of the {{SVGAttr("href")}} or the deprecated {{SVGAttr("xlink:href")}} attribute to reference another gradient, the gradient uses the property's value from the gradient element which is directly referenced by the {{SVGAttr("fill")}} or {{SVGAttr("stroke")}} property. When animating colors, color interpolation is performed according to the value of the `color-interpolation` property on the element being animated.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute, {{CSSXref("color-interpolation")}} can be used as a CSS property.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [a](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/a)
- [animate](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animate)
- [circle](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/circle)
- [clipPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/clipPath)
- [defs](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/defs)
- [ellipse](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/ellipse)
- [foreignObject](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/foreignObject)
- [g](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/g)
- [glyph](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/glyph)
- [image](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/image)
- [line](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/line)
- [linearGradient](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/linearGradient)
- [marker](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/marker)
- [mask](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/mask)
- [missing-glyph](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/missing-glyph)
- [path](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/path)
- [pattern](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/pattern)
- [polygon](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polygon)
- [polyline](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polyline)
- [radialGradient](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/radialGradient)
- [rect](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/rect)
- [svg](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/svg)
- [switch](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/switch)
- [symbol](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/symbol)
- [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text)
- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
- [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan)
- [use](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/use)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>color-interpolation</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.stop-opacity</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>stop</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`stop-opacity`** attribute defines the opacity of a given color gradient stop.

The opacity value used for the gradient calculation is the product of the value of `stop-opacity` and the opacity of the value of the {{SVGAttr("stop-color")}} attribute. For `stop-color` values that don't include explicit opacity information, the opacity is treated as `1`.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute, `stop-opacity` can be used as a CSS property.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [stop](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/stop)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>stop-opacity</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.v-hanging</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>font-face</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`v-hanging`** attribute indicates the alignment coordinate for {{Glossary("glyph", "glyphs")}} to achieve hanging {{Glossary("baseline/typography", "baseline")}} alignment. The value is an offset in the font coordinate system relative to the glyph-specific {{SVGAttr("vert-origin-x")}} attribute.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [font-face](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/font-face)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>True</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>v-hanging</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.end</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>animate animateMotion animateTransform set</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`end`** attribute defines an end value for the animation that can constrain the active duration.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [animate](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animate)
- [animateMotion](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateMotion)
- [animateTransform](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateTransform)
- [set](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/set)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
