  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.maskContentUnits</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>mask mask mask mask</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`maskContentUnits`** attribute indicates which coordinate system to use for the contents of the {{ SVGElement("mask") }} element.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [mask](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/mask)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;mask id="myMask1" maskContentUnits="userSpaceOnUse"&gt;
    &lt;rect fill="black" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%" /&gt;
    &lt;circle fill="white" cx="50" cy="50" r="35" /&gt;
  &lt;/mask&gt;

  &lt;mask id="myMask2" maskContentUnits="objectBoundingBox"&gt;
    &lt;rect fill="black" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%" /&gt;
    &lt;circle fill="white" cx=".5" cy=".5" r=".35" /&gt;
  &lt;/mask&gt;

  &lt;!-- Some reference rect to materialized the mask --&gt;
  &lt;rect id="r1" x="0" y="0" width="45" height="45" /&gt;
  &lt;rect id="r2" x="0" y="55" width="45" height="45" /&gt;
  &lt;rect id="r3" x="55" y="55" width="45" height="45" /&gt;
  &lt;rect id="r4" x="55" y="0" width="45" height="45" /&gt;

  &lt;!-- The first 3 rect are masked with useSpaceOnUse units --&gt;
  &lt;use mask="url(#myMask1)" href="#r1" fill="red" /&gt;
  &lt;use mask="url(#myMask1)" href="#r2" fill="red" /&gt;
  &lt;use mask="url(#myMask1)" href="#r3" fill="red" /&gt;

  &lt;!-- The last rect is masked with objectBoundingBox units --&gt;
  &lt;use mask="url(#myMask2)" href="#r4" fill="red" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>maskContentUnits</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.overflow</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>svg svg pattern marker foreignObject iframe image marker pattern symbol svg text</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`overflow`** attribute sets what to do when an element's content is too big to fit in its block formatting context. **This feature is not widely implemented yet**.

This attribute has the same parameter values and meaning as the {{cssxref("overflow", "CSS overflow property")}}, however, the following additional points apply:

- If it has a value of `visible`, the attribute has no effect (i.e., a clipping rectangle is not created).
- If the `overflow` property has the value `hidden` or `scroll`, a clip of the exact size of the SVG viewport is applied.
- When `scroll` is specified on an [svg](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/svg) element, a scrollbar or panner is normally shown for the SVG viewport whether or not any of its content is clipped.
- Within SVG content, the value `auto` implies that all rendered content for child elements must be visible, either through a scrolling mechanism, or by rendering with no clip.

&gt; **Note:** Although the initial value for overflow is `auto`, it is overwritten in the User Agent style sheet for the [svg](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/svg) element when it is not the root element of a stand-alone document, the [pattern](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/pattern) element, and the [marker](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/marker) element to be hidden by default.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute, `overflow` can be used as a CSS property. See the CSS {{cssxref("overflow")}} property for more information.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [foreignObject](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/foreignObject)
- [iframe](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/iframe)
- [image](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/image)
- [marker](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/marker)
- [pattern](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/pattern)
- [symbol](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/symbol)
- [svg](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/svg)
- [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 200 30" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" overflow="auto"&gt;
  &lt;text y="20"&gt;
    This text is wider than the SVG, so there should be a scrollbar shown.
  &lt;/text&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>overflow</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.markerWidth</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>marker marker marker</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`markerWidth`** attribute represents the width of the viewport into which the [marker](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/marker) is to be fitted when it is rendered according to the {{SVGAttr("viewBox")}} and {{SVGAttr("preserveAspectRatio")}} attributes.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [marker](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/marker)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>markerWidth</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.stroke-width</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>circle ellipse line path polygon polyline rect text textPath tref tspan</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`stroke-width`** attribute is a presentation attribute defining the width of the stroke to be applied to the shape.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [circle](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/circle)
- [ellipse](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/ellipse)
- [line](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/line)
- [path](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/path)
- [polygon](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polygon)
- [polyline](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polyline)
- [rect](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/rect)
- [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text)
- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
- [tref](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tref)
- [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 30 10" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;!-- Default stroke width: 1 --&gt;
  &lt;circle cx="5" cy="5" r="3" stroke="green" /&gt;

  &lt;!-- Stroke width as a number --&gt;
  &lt;circle cx="15" cy="5" r="3" stroke="green" stroke-width="3" /&gt;

  &lt;!-- Stroke width as a percentage --&gt;
  &lt;circle cx="25" cy="5" r="3" stroke="green" stroke-width="2%" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>stroke-width</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.targetX</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>feConvolveMatrix</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`targetX`** attribute determines the positioning in horizontal direction of the convolution matrix relative to a given target pixel in the input image. The leftmost column of the matrix is column number zero. The value must be such that: `0` &lt;= `targetX` &lt; {{SVGAttr("order")}} `X`.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feConvolveMatrix](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feConvolveMatrix)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
