    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.pathLength</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>circle ellipse line path polygon polyline rect circle ellipse line path polygon polyline rect</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`pathLength`** attribute lets authors specify a total length for the path, in user units. This value is then used to calibrate the browser's distance calculations with those of the author, by scaling all distance computations using the ratio `pathLength` / (_computed value of path length_).

This can affect the actual rendered lengths of paths; including text paths, animation paths, and various stroke operations. Basically, all computations that require the length of the path. {{SVGAttr('stroke-dasharray')}}, for example, will assume the start of the path being 0 and the end point the value defined in the `pathLength` attribute.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [circle](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/circle)
- [ellipse](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/ellipse)
- [line](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/line)
- [path](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/path)
- [polygon](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polygon)
- [polyline](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polyline)
- [rect](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/rect)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 100 60" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;style&gt;
    path {
      fill: none;
      stroke: black;
      stroke-width: 2;
      stroke-dasharray: 10;
    }
  &lt;/style&gt;

  &lt;!-- No pathLength, the real length of the path is used. In that case, 100 user units --&gt;
  &lt;path d="M 0,10 h100" /&gt;

  &lt;!-- compute everything like if the path length was 90 user units long --&gt;
  &lt;path d="M 0,20 h100" pathLength="90" /&gt;

  &lt;!-- compute everything like if the path length was 50 user units long --&gt;
  &lt;path d="M 0,30 h100" pathLength="50" /&gt;

  &lt;!-- compute everything like if the path length was 30 user units long --&gt;
  &lt;path d="M 0,40 h100" pathLength="30" /&gt;

  &lt;!-- compute everything like if the path length was 10 user units long --&gt;
  &lt;path d="M 0,50 h100" pathLength="10" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>pathLength</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.min</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>animate animateMotion animateTransform set</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`min`** attribute specifies the minimum value of the active animation duration.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [animate](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animate)
- [animateMotion](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateMotion)
- [animateTransform](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateTransform)
- [set](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/set)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;circle cx="60" cy="10" r="10"&gt;
    &lt;animate
      attributeName="cx"
      dur="4s"
      min="2s"
      repeatCount="indefinite"
      values="60 ; 110 ; 60 ; 10 ; 60"
      keyTimes="0 ; 0.25 ; 0.5 ; 0.75 ; 1" /&gt;
    &lt;animate
      attributeName="cy"
      dur="4s"
      min="2s"
      repeatCount="indefinite"
      values="10 ; 60 ; 110 ; 60 ; 10"
      keyTimes="0 ; 0.25 ; 0.5 ; 0.75 ; 1" /&gt;
  &lt;/circle&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>min</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.xml:space</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>
        </Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Coreattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

SVG supports the built-in XML **`xml:space`** attribute to handle whitespace characters inside elements. Child elements inside an element may also have an `xml:space` attribute that overrides the parent's one.

&gt; **Note:** Instead of using the `xml:space` attribute, use the {{cssxref("white-space")}} CSS property.

This attribute influences how browsers parse text content and therefore changes the way the {{Glossary("DOM")}} is built. Therefore, changing this attribute's value through the DOM API may have no effect.
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>True</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>xml:space</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.font-family</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>text textPath tref tspan</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`font-family`** attribute indicates which font family will be used to render the text, specified as a prioritized list of font family names and/or generic family names.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute, `font-family` can be used as a CSS property. See the {{cssxref("font-family", "CSS font-family")}} property for more information.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text)
- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
- [tref](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tref)
- [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 200 30" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;text y="20" font-family="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Sans serif&lt;/text&gt;
  &lt;text x="100" y="20" font-family="monospace"&gt;Monospace&lt;/text&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>font-family</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.clipPathUnits</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>clipPath clipPath clipPath clipPath</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`clipPathUnits`** attribute indicates which coordinate system to use for the contents of the {{ SVGElement("clipPath") }} element.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [clipPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/clipPath)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 100 100"&gt;
  &lt;clipPath id="myClip1" clipPathUnits="userSpaceOnUse"&gt;
    &lt;circle cx="50" cy="50" r="35" /&gt;
  &lt;/clipPath&gt;

  &lt;clipPath id="myClip2" clipPathUnits="objectBoundingBox"&gt;
    &lt;circle cx=".5" cy=".5" r=".35" /&gt;
  &lt;/clipPath&gt;

  &lt;!-- Some reference rect to materialized to clip path --&gt;
  &lt;rect id="r1" x="0" y="0" width="45" height="45" /&gt;
  &lt;rect id="r2" x="0" y="55" width="45" height="45" /&gt;
  &lt;rect id="r3" x="55" y="55" width="45" height="45" /&gt;
  &lt;rect id="r4" x="55" y="0" width="45" height="45" /&gt;

  &lt;!-- The first 3 rect are clipped with userSpaceOnUse units --&gt;
  &lt;use clip-path="url(#myClip1)" href="#r1" fill="red" /&gt;
  &lt;use clip-path="url(#myClip1)" href="#r2" fill="red" /&gt;
  &lt;use clip-path="url(#myClip1)" href="#r3" fill="red" /&gt;

  &lt;!-- The last rect is clipped with objectBoundingBox units --&gt;
  &lt;use clip-path="url(#myClip2)" href="#r4" fill="red" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>clipPathUnits</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.xlink:href</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>a animate animateMotion animateTransform cursor feImage filter font-face-uri glyphRef image linearGradient mpath pattern radialGradient script set textPath tref use a animate animateMotion animateTransform set cursor feImage filter font-face-uri glyphRef glyph image linearGradient radialGradient mpath path pattern radialGradient linearGradient script textPath path use tref</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>XLinkattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`xlink:href`** attribute defines a reference to a resource as a reference [IRI](/en-US/docs/Web/SVG/Content_type#iri). The exact meaning of that link depends on the context of each element using it.

&gt; **Note:** SVG 2 removed the need for the `xlink` namespace, so instead of `xlink:href` you should use {{SVGAttr("href")}}. If you need to support earlier browser versions, the deprecated `xlink:href` attribute can be used as a fallback in addition to the `href` attribute, e.g. `&lt;use href="some-id" xlink:href="some-id" x="5" y="5" /&gt;`.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [a](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/a)
- [animate](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animate)
- [animateMotion](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateMotion)
- [animateTransform](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateTransform)
- [cursor](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/cursor)
- [feImage](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feImage)
- [filter](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/filter)
- [font-face-uri](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/font-face-uri)
- [glyphRef](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/glyphRef)
- [image](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/image)
- [linearGradient](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/linearGradient)
- [mpath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/mpath)
- [pattern](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/pattern)
- [radialGradient](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/radialGradient)
- [script](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/script)
- [set](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/set)
- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
- [tref](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tref)
- [use](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/use)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 160 40" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;a xlink:href="https://developer.mozilla.org/"&gt;
    &lt;text x="10" y="25"&gt;MDN Web Docs&lt;/text&gt;
  &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>True</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>xlink:href</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.font-size</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>text textPath tref tspan</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`font-size`** attribute refers to the size of the font from {{Glossary("baseline/typography", "baseline")}} to baseline when multiple lines of text are set solid in a multiline layout environment.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute, `font-size` can be used as a CSS property. See the {{cssxref("font-size", "CSS font-size")}} property for more information.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text)
- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
- [tref](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tref)
- [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 200 30" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;text y="20" font-size="smaller"&gt;smaller&lt;/text&gt;
  &lt;text x="100" y="20" font-size="2em"&gt;2em&lt;/text&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>font-size</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.stemv</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>font-face</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`stemv`** attribute indicates the vertical stem width of the font.

The vertical stem width is the width of vertical (or near-vertical) stems of {{Glossary("glyphs")}}. This information is often tied to hinting, and may not be directly accessible in some font formats. The measurement is meant for the dominant vertical stem in the font because there might be different groupings of vertical stems (e.g., one main one, and one lighter weight one as for an uppercase "M" or "N").

If this attribute is used, the {{SVGAttr("units-per-em")}} must also be used.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [font-face](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/font-face)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>True</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>stemv</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.horiz-origin-x</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>font</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`horiz-origin-x`** attribute indicates the x-coordinate in the font coordinate system of the origin of a {{Glossary("glyph")}} to be used when drawing horizontally oriented text.

&gt; **Note:** The origin applies to all glyphs in the font.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [font](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/font)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>True</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>horiz-origin-x</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.filter</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>filter defs use filter</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`filter`** attribute specifies the filter effects defined by the [filter](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/filter) element that shall be applied to its element.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute, `filter` can be used as a CSS property. See {{cssxref("filter", "CSS filter")}} for further information.

As a presentation attribute, it can be applied to any element but it only has effect on [container elements](/en-US/docs/Web/SVG/Element#container_elements) without the [defs](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/defs) element, all [graphics elements](/en-US/docs/Web/SVG/Element#graphics_elements) and the [use](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/use) element.
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;filter id="blur"&gt;
    &lt;feGaussianBlur stdDeviation="2" /&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;

  &lt;rect x="10" y="10" width="80" height="80" filter="url(#blur)" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>filter</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.font-style</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>text textPath tref tspan</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`font-style`** attribute specifies whether the text is to be rendered using a normal, italic, or oblique face.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute, `font-style` can be used as a CSS property. See the {{cssxref("font-style", "CSS font-style")}} property for more information.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text)
- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
- [tref](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tref)
- [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 250 30" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;text y="20" font-style="normal"&gt;Normal font style&lt;/text&gt;
  &lt;text x="150" y="20" font-style="italic"&gt;Italic font style&lt;/text&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>font-style</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
