  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.dy</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>feDropShadow feOffset glyphRef text tref tspan feDropShadow filter feOffset filter glyphRef glyphRef text tref tref tspan</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`dy`** attribute indicates a shift along the y-axis on the position of an element or its content.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feDropShadow](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feDropShadow)
- [feOffset](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feOffset)
- [glyphRef](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/glyphRef)
- [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text)
- [tref](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tref)
- [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;!-- Lines materialized the position of the glyphs --&gt;
  &lt;line x1="10%" x2="10%" y1="0" y2="100%" /&gt;
  &lt;line x1="0" x2="100%" y1="30%" y2="30%" /&gt;
  &lt;line x1="0" x2="100%" y1="80%" y2="80%" /&gt;

  &lt;!-- Some reference text --&gt;
  &lt;text x="10%" y="30%" fill="grey"&gt;SVG&lt;/text&gt;

  &lt;!-- The same text with a shift along the y-axis --&gt;
  &lt;text dy="50%" x="10%" y="30%"&gt;SVG&lt;/text&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```
```css
line {
  stroke: red;
  stroke-width: 0.5px;
  stroke-dasharray: 3px;
}
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>dy</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.kerning</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>textPath text tref tspan</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`kerning`** attribute indicates whether the spacing between {{Glossary("glyph", "glyphs")}} should be adjusted based on kerning tables that are included in the relevant font (i.e., enable auto-kerning) or instead disable auto-kerning and set the spacing between them to a specific length (typically, zero).

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute `kerning` can be used as a CSS property. In CSS the property is called {{cssxref("font-kerning")}}, though.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
- [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text)
- [tref](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tref)
- [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
  font:
    36px Verdana,
    Helvetica,
    Arial,
    sans-serif;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 150 125" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;text x="10" y="30" kerning="auto"&gt;auto&lt;/text&gt;
  &lt;text x="10" y="70" kerning="0"&gt;number&lt;/text&gt;
  &lt;text x="10" y="110" kerning="20px"&gt;length&lt;/text&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>True</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>kerning</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.cy</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>circle ellipse radialGradient circle ellipse radialGradient</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`cy`** attribute define the y-axis coordinate of a center point.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [circle](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/circle)
- [ellipse](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/ellipse)
- [radialGradient](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/radialGradient)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 100 300" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;radialGradient cy="25%" id="myGradient"&gt;
    &lt;stop offset="0" stop-color="white" /&gt;
    &lt;stop offset="100%" stop-color="black" /&gt;
  &lt;/radialGradient&gt;

  &lt;circle cy="50" cx="50" r="45" /&gt;
  &lt;ellipse cy="150" cx="50" rx="45" ry="25" /&gt;
  &lt;rect x="5" y="205" width="90" height="90" fill="url(#myGradient)" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>cy</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.word-spacing</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>text textPath tref tspan text</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`word-spacing`** attribute specifies spacing behavior between words.

If a {{cssxref("length")}} is provided without a unit identifier (e.g. an unqualified number such as 128), the browser processes the \&lt;length&gt; as a width value in the current user coordinate system.

If a \&lt;length&gt; is provided with one of the unit identifiers (e.g. .25em or 1%), then the browser converts the \&lt;length&gt; into a corresponding value in the current user coordinate system.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute, `word-spacing` can be used as a CSS property. See the {{cssxref("word-spacing", "CSS word-spacing")}} property for more information.
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>word-spacing</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.ry</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>ellipse rect ellipse rect</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`ry`** attribute defines a radius on the y-axis.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [ellipse](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/ellipse)
- [rect](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/rect)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 300 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;ellipse cx="50" cy="50" ry="0" rx="25" /&gt;
  &lt;ellipse cx="150" cy="50" ry="25" rx="25" /&gt;
  &lt;ellipse cx="250" cy="50" ry="50" rx="25" /&gt;

  &lt;rect x="20" y="120" width="60" height="60" ry="0" rx="15" /&gt;
  &lt;rect x="120" y="120" width="60" height="60" ry="15" rx="15" /&gt;
  &lt;rect x="220" y="120" width="60" height="60" ry="150" rx="15" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>ry</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.restart</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>animate animateMotion animateTransform set</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`restart`** attribute specifies whether or not an animation can restart.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [animate](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animate)
- [animateMotion](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateMotion)
- [animateTransform](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateTransform)
- [set](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/set)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}

a {
  fill: blue;
  text-decoration: underline;
  cursor: pointer;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 220 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;rect y="30" width="100" height="100"&gt;
    &lt;animate
      attributeType="XML"
      attributeName="y"
      from="30"
      to="100"
      dur="5s"
      repeatCount="1"
      restart="always" /&gt;
  &lt;/rect&gt;
  &lt;rect x="120" y="30" width="100" height="100"&gt;
    &lt;animate
      attributeType="XML"
      attributeName="y"
      from="30"
      to="100"
      dur="5s"
      repeatCount="1"
      restart="whenNotActive" /&gt;
  &lt;/rect&gt;
  &lt;a id="restart"&gt;&lt;text y="20"&gt;Restart animation&lt;/text&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```
```js
document.getElementById("restart").addEventListener("click", (evt) =&gt; {
  document.querySelectorAll("animate").forEach((element) =&gt; {
    element.beginElement();
  });
});
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>restart</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.calcMode</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>animate animateMotion animateTransform animateMotion animateMotion</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Animationvalueattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`calcMode`** attribute specifies the {{Glossary("interpolation")}} mode for the animation.

The default mode is `linear`, however if the attribute does not support linear interpolation (e.g. for strings), the `calcMode` attribute is ignored and discrete interpolation is used.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [animate](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animate)
- [animateMotion](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateMotion)
- [animateTransform](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateTransform)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>calcMode</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.glyph-orientation-horizontal</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>textPath text tref tspan</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`glyph-orientation-horizontal`** attribute affects the amount that the current text position advances as each {{Glossary("glyph")}} is rendered.

When the reference orientation direction is horizontal and the `glyph-orientation-horizontal` results in an orientation angle that is a multiple of 180 degrees, then the current text position is incremented according to the horizontal metrics of the glyph. Otherwise, if the value of this attribute is not a multiple of 180 degrees, then the current text position is incremented according to the vertical metrics of the glyph.

This attribute is applied only to text written in a horizontal {{SVGAttr("writing-mode")}}.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute, `glyph-orientation-horizontal` can be used as a CSS property.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
- [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text)
- [tref](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tref)
- [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>True</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>glyph-orientation-horizontal</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.keyPoints</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>animate animateMotion animateTransform set</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`keyPoints`** attribute indicates the simple duration of an animation.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [animate](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animate)
- [animateMotion](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateMotion)
- [animateTransform](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateTransform)
- [set](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/set)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg
  viewBox="0 0 120 120"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"&gt;
  &lt;path
    d="M10,110 A120,120 -45 0,1 110 10 A120,120 -45 0,1 10,110"
    stroke="lightgrey"
    stroke-width="2"
    fill="none"
    id="motionPath" /&gt;
  &lt;circle cx="10" cy="110" r="3" fill="lightgrey" /&gt;
  &lt;circle cx="110" cy="10" r="3" fill="lightgrey" /&gt;

  &lt;circle r="5" fill="red"&gt;
    &lt;animateMotion
      dur="3s"
      repeatCount="indefinite"
      keyPoints="0;0.5;1"
      keyTimes="0;0.15;1"
      calcMode="linear"&gt;
      &lt;mpath href="#motionPath" /&gt;
    &lt;/animateMotion&gt;
  &lt;/circle&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
