  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.writing-mode</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>text text textPath tref tspan</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`writing-mode`** attribute specifies whether the initial inline-progression-direction for a [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text) element shall be left-to-right, right-to-left, or top-to-bottom. The `writing-mode` attribute applies only to {{ SVGElement("text") }} elements; the attribute is ignored for {{ SVGElement("tspan") }}, {{ SVGElement("tref") }}, and {{ SVGElement("textPath") }} sub-elements. (Note that the inline-progression-direction can change within a {{ SVGElement("text") }} element due to the Unicode bidirectional algorithm and properties {{ SVGAttr("direction") }} and {{ SVGAttr("unicode-bidi") }}.)

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute, `writing-mode` can be used as a CSS property. See the CSS {{cssxref("writing-mode")}} property for more information.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text)
- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
- [tref](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tref)
- [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>writing-mode</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.pointer-events</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>a circle clipPath defs ellipse foreignObject g image line marker mask path pattern polygon polyline rect svg switch symbol text textPath tspan use</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`pointer-events`** attribute is a presentation attribute that allows defining whether or when an element may be the target of a mouse event.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute {{cssxref('pointer-events')}} can be used as a CSS property.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [a](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/a)
- [circle](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/circle)
- [clipPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/clipPath)
- [defs](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/defs)
- [ellipse](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/ellipse)
- [foreignObject](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/foreignObject)
- [g](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/g)
- [image](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/image)
- [line](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/line)
- [marker](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/marker)
- [mask](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/mask)
- [path](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/path)
- [pattern](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/pattern)
- [polygon](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polygon)
- [polyline](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polyline)
- [rect](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/rect)
- [svg](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/svg)
- [switch](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/switch)
- [symbol](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/symbol)
- [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text)
- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
- [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan)
- [use](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/use)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 20 10" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;!--
  The circle will always intercept the mouse event.
  To change the color of the rect underneath you have
  to click outside the circle
  --&gt;
  &lt;rect x="0" y="0" height="10" width="10" fill="black" /&gt;
  &lt;circle cx="5" cy="5" r="4" fill="white" pointer-events="visiblePainted" /&gt;

  &lt;!--
  The circle below will never catch a mouse event.
  The rect underneath will change color whether you
  are clicking on the circle or the rect itself
  --&gt;
  &lt;rect x="10" y="0" height="10" width="10" fill="black" /&gt;
  &lt;circle cx="15" cy="5" r="4" fill="white" pointer-events="none" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```
```js
window.addEventListener("mouseup", (e) =&gt; {
  // Let's pick a random color between #000000 and #FFFFFF
  const color = Math.round(Math.random() * 0xffffff);

  // Let's format the color to fit CSS requirements
  const fill = `#${color.toString(16).padStart(6, "0")}`;

  // Let's apply our color in the
  // element we actually clicked on
  e.target.style.fill = fill;
});
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>pointer-events</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.repeatCount</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>animate animateMotion animateTransform set</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`repeatCount`** attribute indicates the number of times an animation will take place.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [animate](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animate)
- [animateMotion](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateMotion)
- [animateTransform](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateTransform)
- [set](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/set)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 220 150" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;rect x="0" y="0" width="100" height="100"&gt;
    &lt;animate
      attributeType="XML"
      attributeName="y"
      from="0"
      to="50"
      dur="1s"
      repeatCount="5" /&gt;
  &lt;/rect&gt;
  &lt;rect x="120" y="0" width="100" height="100"&gt;
    &lt;animate
      attributeType="XML"
      attributeName="y"
      from="0"
      to="50"
      dur="1s"
      repeatCount="indefinite" /&gt;
  &lt;/rect&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>repeatCount</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.k4</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>feComposite feComposite</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`k4`** attribute defines one of the values to be used within the `arithmetic` operation of the [feComposite](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feComposite) filter primitive.

The pixel composition is computed using the following formula:

```plain
result = k1*i1*i2 + k2*i1 + k3*i2 + k4
```

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feComposite](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feComposite)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 420 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;filter id="composite1" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feComposite
      in2="SourceGraphic"
      operator="arithmetic"
      k1="1"
      k2="0"
      k3="0"
      k4="0" /&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;
  &lt;filter id="composite2" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feComposite
      in2="SourceGraphic"
      operator="arithmetic"
      k1="10"
      k2="0"
      k3="0"
      k4="0.3" /&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;

  &lt;image
    href="mdn.svg"
    x="0"
    y="0"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    style="filter: url(#composite1);" /&gt;
  &lt;image
    href="mdn.svg"
    x="0"
    y="0"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    style="filter: url(#composite2); transform: translateX(220px);" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>k4</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.divisor</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>feConvolveMatrix feConvolveMatrix</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`divisor`** attribute specifies the value by which the resulting number of applying the {{SVGAttr("kernelMatrix")}} of a [feConvolveMatrix](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feConvolveMatrix) element to the input image color value is divided to yield the destination color value.

A divisor that is the sum of all the matrix values tends to have an evening effect on the overall color intensity of the result.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feConvolveMatrix](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feConvolveMatrix)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 420 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;filter id="convolveMatrix1" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feConvolveMatrix kernelMatrix="1 2 0 0 0 0 0 0 -1" divisor="1" /&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;
  &lt;filter id="convolveMatrix2" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feConvolveMatrix kernelMatrix="1 2 0 0 0 0 0 0 -1" divisor="8" /&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;

  &lt;image
    href="mdn_logo_only_color.png"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    style="filter:url(#convolveMatrix1);" /&gt;
  &lt;image
    href="mdn_logo_only_color.png"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    style="filter:url(#convolveMatrix2); transform:translateX(220px);" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>divisor</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
