      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`additive`** attribute controls whether or not an animation is additive.

It is frequently useful to define animation as an offset or delta to an attribute's value, rather than as absolute values.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [animate](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animate)
- [animateMotion](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateMotion)
- [animateTransform](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateTransform)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>additive</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.to</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>animate animateMotion animateTransform set animate animateMotion animateTransform set</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`to`** attribute indicates the final value of the attribute that will be modified during the animation.

The value of the attribute will change between the {{SVGAttr("from")}} attribute value and this value.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [animate](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animate)
- [animateMotion](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateMotion)
- [animateTransform](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateTransform)
- [set](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/set)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 200 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;rect x="10" y="10" width="100" height="100"&gt;
    &lt;animate
      attributeType="XML"
      attributeName="width"
      fill="freeze"
      from="100"
      to="150"
      dur="3s" /&gt;
  &lt;/rect&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>to</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.image-rendering</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>image</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`image-rendering`** attribute provides a hint to the browser about how to make speed vs. quality tradeoffs as it performs image processing.

The resampling is always done in a truecolor (e.g., 24-bit) color space even if the original data and/or the target device is indexed color.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute, `image-rendering` can be used as a CSS property. See the {{cssxref("image-rendering", "CSS image-rendering")}} property for more information.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [image](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/image)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>image-rendering</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.baseFrequency</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>feTurbulence feTurbulence</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`baseFrequency`** attribute represents the base frequency parameter for the noise function of the [feTurbulence](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feTurbulence) filter primitive.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feTurbulence](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feTurbulence)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 420 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;filter id="noise1" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feTurbulence baseFrequency="0.025" /&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;
  &lt;filter id="noise2" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feTurbulence baseFrequency="0.05" /&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;

  &lt;rect x="0" y="0" width="200" height="200" style="filter: url(#noise1);" /&gt;
  &lt;rect
    x="0"
    y="0"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    style="filter: url(#noise2); transform: translateX(220px);" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>baseFrequency</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.exponent</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>feFuncA feFuncB feFuncG feFuncR</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`exponent`** attribute defines the exponent of the gamma function.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feFuncA](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feFuncA)
- [feFuncB](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feFuncB)
- [feFuncG](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feFuncG)
- [feFuncR](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feFuncR)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 420 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;defs&gt;
    &lt;linearGradient
      id="gradient"
      gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse"
      x1="0"
      y1="0"
      x2="200"
      y2="0"&gt;
      &lt;stop offset="0" stop-color="#ff0000" /&gt;
      &lt;stop offset="0.5" stop-color="#00ff00" /&gt;
      &lt;stop offset="1" stop-color="#0000ff" /&gt;
    &lt;/linearGradient&gt;
  &lt;/defs&gt;

  &lt;filter id="componentTransfer1" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feComponentTransfer&gt;
      &lt;feFuncR type="gamma" exponent="1" /&gt;
      &lt;feFuncG type="gamma" exponent="1" /&gt;
      &lt;feFuncB type="gamma" exponent="1" /&gt;
    &lt;/feComponentTransfer&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;
  &lt;filter id="componentTransfer2" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feComponentTransfer&gt;
      &lt;feFuncR type="gamma" exponent="5" /&gt;
      &lt;feFuncG type="gamma" exponent="5" /&gt;
      &lt;feFuncB type="gamma" exponent="5" /&gt;
    &lt;/feComponentTransfer&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;

  &lt;rect
    x="0"
    y="0"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    fill="url(#gradient)"
    style="filter: url(#componentTransfer1);" /&gt;
  &lt;rect
    x="0"
    y="0"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    fill="url(#gradient)"
    style="filter: url(#componentTransfer2); transform: translateX(220px);" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>exponent</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.paint-order</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>circle ellipse line path polygon polyline rect text textPath tspan</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`paint-order`** attribute specifies the order that the fill, stroke, and markers of a given shape or text element are painted.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute, `paint-order` can be used as a CSS property.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [circle](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/circle)
- [ellipse](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/ellipse)
- [line](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/line)
- [path](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/path)
- [polygon](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polygon)
- [polyline](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polyline)
- [rect](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/rect)
- [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text)
- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
- [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>paint-order</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.primitiveUnits</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>filter filter filter</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`primitiveUnits`** attribute specifies the coordinate system for the various length values within the filter primitives and for the attributes that define the filter primitive subregion.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [filter](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/filter)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>primitiveUnits</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.target</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>a</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`target`** attribute should be used when there are multiple possible targets for the ending resource, such as when the parent document is embedded within an HTML or XHTML document, or is viewed with a tabbed browser. This attribute specifies the name of the browsing context (e.g., a browser tab or an (X)HTML iframe or object element) into which a document is to be opened when the link is activated:

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [a](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/a)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}

text {
  font:
    20px Arial,
    Helvetica,
    sans-serif;
  fill: blue;
  text-decoration: underline;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 300 120" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;a href="https://developer.mozilla.org" target="_self"&gt;
    &lt;text x="0" y="20"&gt;Open link within iframe&lt;/text&gt;
  &lt;/a&gt;
  &lt;a href="https://developer.mozilla.org" target="_blank"&gt;
    &lt;text x="0" y="60"&gt;Open link in new tab or window&lt;/text&gt;
  &lt;/a&gt;
  &lt;a href="https://developer.mozilla.org" target="_top"&gt;
    &lt;text x="0" y="100"&gt;Open link in this tab or window&lt;/text&gt;
  &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>target</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.preserveAspectRatio</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>image svg symbol image feImage marker pattern view feImage image marker pattern svg symbol view</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`preserveAspectRatio`** attribute indicates how an element with a viewBox providing a given {{glossary("aspect ratio")}} must fit into a viewport with a different aspect ratio.

The aspect ratio of an SVG image is defined by the {{SVGAttr('viewBox')}} attribute. Therefore, if `viewBox` isn't set, the `preserveAspectRatio` attribute has no effect on SVG's scaling (except in the case of the [image](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/image) element, where `preserveAspectRatio` behaves differently as described below).
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>preserveAspectRatio</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.gradientTransform</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>linearGradient radialGradient</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The `gradientTransform` attribute contains the definition of an optional additional transformation from the gradient coordinate system onto the target coordinate system (i.e., userSpaceOnUse or objectBoundingBox). This allows for things such as skewing the gradient. This additional transformation matrix is post-multiplied to (i.e., inserted to the right of) any previously defined transformations, including the implicit transformation necessary to convert from object bounding box units to user space.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [linearGradient](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/linearGradient)
- [radialGradient](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/radialGradient)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 420 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;radialGradient
    id="gradient1"
    gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse"
    cx="100"
    cy="100"
    r="100"
    fx="100"
    fy="100"&gt;
    &lt;stop offset="0%" stop-color="darkblue" /&gt;
    &lt;stop offset="50%" stop-color="skyblue" /&gt;
    &lt;stop offset="100%" stop-color="darkblue" /&gt;
  &lt;/radialGradient&gt;
  &lt;radialGradient
    id="gradient2"
    gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse"
    cx="100"
    cy="100"
    r="100"
    fx="100"
    fy="100"
    gradientTransform="skewX(20) translate(-35, 0)"&gt;
    &lt;stop offset="0%" stop-color="darkblue" /&gt;
    &lt;stop offset="50%" stop-color="skyblue" /&gt;
    &lt;stop offset="100%" stop-color="darkblue" /&gt;
  &lt;/radialGradient&gt;

  &lt;rect x="0" y="0" width="200" height="200" fill="url(#gradient1)" /&gt;
  &lt;rect
    x="0"
    y="0"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    fill="url(#gradient2)"
    style="transform: translateX(220px);" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>gradientTransform</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.values</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>animate animateMotion animateTransform feColorMatrix animate animateMotion animateTransform feColorMatrix</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The `values` attribute has different meanings, depending upon the context where it's used, either it defines a sequence of values used over the course of an animation, or it's a list of numbers for a color matrix, which is interpreted differently depending on the type of color change to be performed.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [animate](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animate)
- [animateMotion](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateMotion)
- [animateTransform](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateTransform)
- [feColorMatrix](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feColorMatrix)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>values</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.class</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>
        </Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Coreattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

« [SVG Attribute reference home](/en-US/docs/Web/SVG/Attribute)

Assigns a class name or set of class names to an element. You may assign the same class name or names to any number of elements, however, multiple class names must be separated by whitespace characters.

An element's class name serves two key roles:

- As a style sheet selector, for when an author assigns style information to a set of elements.
- For general use by the browser.

You can use this class to style SVG content using CSS.
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>class</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
