  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.max</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>animate animateMotion animateTransform set</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`max`** attribute specifies the maximum value of the active animation duration.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [animate](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animate)
- [animateMotion](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateMotion)
- [animateTransform](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/animateTransform)
- [set](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/set)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;circle cx="60" cy="10" r="10"&gt;
    &lt;animate
      attributeName="cx"
      dur="4s"
      max="6s"
      repeatCount="indefinite"
      values="60 ; 110 ; 60 ; 10 ; 60"
      keyTimes="0 ; 0.25 ; 0.5 ; 0.75 ; 1" /&gt;
    &lt;animate
      attributeName="cy"
      dur="4s"
      max="6s"
      repeatCount="indefinite"
      values="10 ; 60 ; 110 ; 60 ; 10"
      keyTimes="0 ; 0.25 ; 0.5 ; 0.75 ; 1" /&gt;
  &lt;/circle&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>max</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.targetY</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>feConvolveMatrix</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`targetY`** attribute determines the positioning in vertical direction of the convolution matrix relative to a given target pixel in the input image. The topmost row of the matrix is row number zero. The value must be such that: `0` &lt;= `targetY` &lt; {{SVGAttr("order")}} `Y`.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feConvolveMatrix](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feConvolveMatrix)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>targetY</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.u2</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>glyph hkern vkern</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`u2`** attribute specifies list of {{Glossary("Unicode")}} characters (refer to the description of the {{SVGAttr("unicode")}} attribute of the [glyph](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/glyph) element for a description of how to express individual Unicode characters) and/or ranges of Unicode characters, which identify a set of possible second {{Glossary("glyph")}} in a kerning pair.

If a given Unicode character within the set has multiple corresponding `&lt;glyph&gt;` elements (i.e., there are multiple `&lt;glyph&gt;` elements with the same `unicode` attribute value but different {{SVGAttr("glyph-name")}} values), then all such glyphs are included in the set. Comma is the separator character; thus, to kern a comma, specify the comma as part of a range of Unicode characters or as a glyph name using the {{SVGAttr("g2")}} attribute. The total set of possible second glyphs in the kerning pair is the union of glyphs specified by the `u2` and `g2` attributes.
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>True</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>u2</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.patternTransform</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>pattern pattern</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`patternTransform`** attribute defines a list of [transform definitions](/en-US/docs/Web/SVG/Attribute/transform#transform_functions) that are applied to a pattern tile.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [pattern](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/pattern)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;!-- Apply a transform on the tile --&gt;
  &lt;pattern
    id="p1"
    width=".25"
    height=".25"
    patternTransform="rotate(20)
                      skewX(30)
                      scale(1 0.5)"&gt;
    &lt;circle cx="10" cy="10" r="10" /&gt;
  &lt;/pattern&gt;

  &lt;!-- Apply the transformed pattern tile --&gt;
  &lt;rect x="10" y="10" width="80" height="80" fill="url(#p1)" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>patternTransform</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
