      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.g1</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>hkern vkern glyph</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`g1`** attribute specifies a list of glyph names which identify a set of possible first glyphs in the kerning pair.

All glyphs with the given glyph name are included in the set. The total set of possible first glyphs in the kerning pair is the union of glyphs specified by the {{SVGAttr("u1")}} and `g1` attributes.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [hkern](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/hkern)
- [vkern](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/vkern)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>True</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>g1</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.tableValues</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>feFuncA feFuncB feFuncG feFuncR</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`tableValues`** attribute defines a list of numbers defining a lookup table of values for a color component transfer function.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feFuncA](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feFuncA)
- [feFuncB](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feFuncB)
- [feFuncG](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feFuncG)
- [feFuncR](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feFuncR)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 420 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;defs&gt;
    &lt;linearGradient
      id="gradient"
      gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse"
      x1="0"
      y1="0"
      x2="200"
      y2="0"&gt;
      &lt;stop offset="0" stop-color="#ff0000" /&gt;
      &lt;stop offset="0.5" stop-color="#00ff00" /&gt;
      &lt;stop offset="1" stop-color="#0000ff" /&gt;
    &lt;/linearGradient&gt;
  &lt;/defs&gt;

  &lt;filter id="componentTransfer1" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feComponentTransfer&gt;
      &lt;feFuncR type="table" tableValues="0 1" /&gt;
      &lt;feFuncG type="table" tableValues="0 1" /&gt;
      &lt;feFuncB type="table" tableValues="0 1" /&gt;
    &lt;/feComponentTransfer&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;
  &lt;filter id="componentTransfer2" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feComponentTransfer&gt;
      &lt;feFuncR type="table" tableValues="1 0" /&gt;
      &lt;feFuncG type="table" tableValues="1 0" /&gt;
      &lt;feFuncB type="table" tableValues="1 0" /&gt;
    &lt;/feComponentTransfer&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;

  &lt;rect
    x="0"
    y="0"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    fill="url(#gradient)"
    style="filter: url(#componentTransfer1);" /&gt;
  &lt;rect
    x="0"
    y="0"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    fill="url(#gradient)"
    style="filter: url(#componentTransfer2); transform: translateX(220px);" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>tableValues</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.alignment-baseline</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>tspan tref textPath text</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`alignment-baseline`** attribute specifies how an object is aligned with respect to its parent. This property specifies which baseline of this element is to be aligned with the corresponding baseline of the parent. For example, this allows alphabetic baselines in Roman text to stay aligned across font size changes. It defaults to the baseline with the same name as the computed value of the `alignment-baseline` property.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute `alignment-baseline` can be used as a CSS property.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [tspan](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tspan)
- [tref](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/tref)
- [textPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/textPath)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>alignment-baseline</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.stemh</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>font-face</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`stemh`** attribute indicates the horizontal stem width of the font.

The stem width refers to the dominant stem of the font. There may be two or more designed widths. For example, the main vertical stems of Roman characters will differ from the thin stems on serifed "M" and "N", plus there may be different widths for uppercase and lowercase characters in the same font. Also, either by design or by error, all stems may have slightly different widths.

If this attribute is used, the {{SVGAttr("units-per-em")}} must also be used.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [font-face](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/font-face)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>True</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>stemh</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.intercept</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>feFuncA feFuncB feFuncG feFuncR</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`intercept`** attribute defines the intercept of the linear function of color component transfers when the {{SVGAttr("type")}} attribute is set to `linear`.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feFuncA](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feFuncA)
- [feFuncB](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feFuncB)
- [feFuncG](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feFuncG)
- [feFuncR](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feFuncR)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 420 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;defs&gt;
    &lt;linearGradient
      id="gradient"
      gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse"
      x1="0"
      y1="0"
      x2="200"
      y2="0"&gt;
      &lt;stop offset="0" stop-color="#ff0000" /&gt;
      &lt;stop offset="0.5" stop-color="#00ff00" /&gt;
      &lt;stop offset="1" stop-color="#0000ff" /&gt;
    &lt;/linearGradient&gt;
  &lt;/defs&gt;

  &lt;filter id="componentTransfer1" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feComponentTransfer&gt;
      &lt;feFuncR type="linear" intercept="0" /&gt;
      &lt;feFuncG type="linear" intercept="0" /&gt;
      &lt;feFuncB type="linear" intercept="0" /&gt;
    &lt;/feComponentTransfer&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;
  &lt;filter id="componentTransfer2" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%"&gt;
    &lt;feComponentTransfer&gt;
      &lt;feFuncR type="linear" intercept="0.3" /&gt;
      &lt;feFuncG type="linear" intercept="0.1" /&gt;
      &lt;feFuncB type="linear" intercept="0.8" /&gt;
    &lt;/feComponentTransfer&gt;
  &lt;/filter&gt;

  &lt;rect
    x="0"
    y="0"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    fill="url(#gradient)"
    style="filter: url(#componentTransfer1);" /&gt;
  &lt;rect
    x="0"
    y="0"
    width="200"
    height="200"
    fill="url(#gradient)"
    style="filter: url(#componentTransfer2); transform: translateX(220px);" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>intercept</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.kernelUnitLength</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>feConvolveMatrix feConvolveMatrix feDiffuseLighting feSpecularLighting feConvolveMatrix feDiffuseLighting feSpecularLighting</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`kernelUnitLength`** attribute has two meanings based on the context it's used in. For lighting filter primitives, it indicates the intended distance for the x and y coordinates, for [feConvolveMatrix](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feConvolveMatrix), it indicates the intended distance between successive columns and rows in the kernel matrix.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [feConvolveMatrix](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feConvolveMatrix)
- [feDiffuseLighting](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feDiffuseLighting)
- [feSpecularLighting](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/feSpecularLighting)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>True</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>kernelUnitLength</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.g2</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>hkern vkern glyph</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`g2`** attribute specifies a list of glyph names which identify a set of possible second glyphs in the kerning pair.

All glyphs with the given glyph name are included in the set. The total set of possible second glyphs in the kerning pair is the union of glyphs specified by the {{SVGAttr("u2")}} and `g2` attributes.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [hkern](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/hkern)
- [vkern](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/vkern)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>True</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>g2</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.filterUnits</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>filter filter filter</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`filterUnits`** attribute defines the coordinate system for the attributes {{SVGAttr("x")}}, {{SVGAttr("y")}}, {{SVGAttr("width")}} and {{SVGAttr("height")}}.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [filter](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/filter)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>elements</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
