  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.stop-color</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>stop</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`stop-color`** attribute indicates what color to use at a gradient stop.

&gt; **Note:** With respect to gradients, SVG treats the `transparent` keyword differently than CSS. SVG does not calculate gradients in pre-multiplied space, so `transparent` really means transparent black. So, specifying a `stop-color` with the value `transparent` is equivalent to specifying a `stop-color` with the value `black` and a {{SVGAttr("stop-opacity")}} with the value `0`.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute, `stop-color` can be used as a CSS property.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [stop](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/stop)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>stop-color</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.mask</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>a circle clipPath ellipse g glyph image line marker mask path pattern polygon polyline rect svg symbol text use</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`mask`** attribute is a presentation attribute mainly used to bind a given {{ SVGElement("mask") }} element with the element the attribute belongs to.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute {{cssxref('mask')}} can be used as a CSS property.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [a](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/a)
- [circle](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/circle)
- [clipPath](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/clipPath)
- [ellipse](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/ellipse)
- [g](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/g)
- [glyph](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/glyph)
- [image](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/image)
- [line](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/line)
- [marker](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/marker)
- [mask](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/mask)
- [path](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/path)
- [pattern](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/pattern)
- [polygon](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polygon)
- [polyline](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polyline)
- [rect](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/rect)
- [svg](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/svg)
- [symbol](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/symbol)
- [text](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/text)
- [use](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/use)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 200 100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;mask id="myMask" maskContentUnits="objectBoundingBox"&gt;
    &lt;rect fill="white" x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%" /&gt;
    &lt;polygon
      fill="black"
      points="0.5,0.2 0.68,0.74 0.21,0.41 0.79,0.41 0.32,0.74" /&gt;
  &lt;/mask&gt;

  &lt;!--
  Punch a hole in a shape of a star inside the red circle,
  revealing the yellow circle underneath
  --&gt;
  &lt;circle cx="50" cy="50" r="20" fill="yellow" /&gt;
  &lt;circle cx="50" cy="50" r="45" fill="red" mask="url(#myMask)" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Group</Name>
        <Value>global_attributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>mask</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.shape-rendering</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>circle ellipse line path polygon polyline rect</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Category</Name>
        <Value>Presentationattributes</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`shape-rendering`** attribute provides hints to the renderer about what tradeoffs to make when rendering shapes like paths, circles, or rectangles.

&gt; **Note:** As a presentation attribute, `shape-rendering` can be used as a CSS property.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- [circle](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/circle)
- [ellipse](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/ellipse)
- [line](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/line)
- [path](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/path)
- [polygon](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polygon)
- [polyline](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/polyline)
- [rect](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/rect)
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Example</Name>
        <Value>```css hidden
html,
body,
svg {
  height: 100%;
}
```
```html
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 420 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;
  &lt;circle cx="100" cy="100" r="100" shape-rendering="geometricPrecision" /&gt;
  &lt;circle cx="320" cy="100" r="100" shape-rendering="crispEdges" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;
```</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
