  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.overline-position</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>
        </Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The `overline-position` attribute represents the ideal vertical position of the overline. The overline position is expressed in the font's coordinate system.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- {{ SVGElement("font-face") }}
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>overline-position</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.z</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>filter fePointLight filter feSpotLight filter</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The **`z`** attribute defines the location along the z-axis for a light source in the coordinate system established by the {{SVGAttr("primitiveUnits")}} attribute on the [filter](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/web/svg/element/filter) element, assuming that, in the initial coordinate system, the positive z-axis comes out towards the person viewing the content and assuming that one unit along the z-axis equals one unit in x and y.
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
        <Value>False</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Name</Name>
        <Value>z</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>PSTypeName</Name>
        <Value>SVG.Attribute</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
    </Members>
  </Type>
  <Type>
    <Name>SVG.Attribute.strikethrough-position</Name>
    <Members>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>AppliesTo</Name>
        <Value>
        </Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Description</Name>
        <Value>

{{SVGRef}}

The `strikethrough-position` attribute represents the ideal vertical position of the strikethrough. The strikethrough position is expressed in the font's coordinate system.

You can use this attribute with the following SVG elements:

- {{ SVGElement("font-face") }}
</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>Header</Name>
        <Value>System.Collections.Hashtable</Value>
      </NoteProperty>
      <NoteProperty>
        <Name>IsDeprecated</Name>
